const FICHAS={"sintra-cascais":{"corpo":"<p>Sintra-Cascais Natural Park has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1995 and is one of the most protected territories in the country. The revision of Sintra's Municipal Master Plan, currently under discussion, proposes reclassifying land that is today protected, opening the way to high-rise construction and new developments within the Park's boundaries.</p>\n<p>The Finis Terrae association warns that the proposal threatens ecological corridors, watercourses and the landscape heritage that led to the mountain range's international classification. The public petition delivered to Parliament already has over 7,000 signatures.</p>\n<p>The Master Plan revision remains under public consultation, with information sessions scheduled throughout the year.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT132295"],["Finis Terrae","https://finisterrae.pt"],["Notícias de Lisboa","https://noticiaslx.pt/2026/07/25/peticao-contesta-urbanizacao-prevista-no-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais-na-revisao-do-pdm/"]],"stat":"7,000+ signatures","link":"https://finisterrae.pt","linkL":"Learn more at finisterrae.pt"},"barroso":{"corpo":"<p>British company Savannah Resources wants to open an open-pit lithium mine in a centuries-old farming area, classified as a Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System by the FAO. Covas do Barroso has resisted the project for eight years.</p>\n<p>From August 6 to 10, 2026, between 700 and 800 people take part in the Camp in Defence of Barroso, organized by Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso with support from A Sachola, Disgraça and Jornal Mapa.</p>\n<p>In parallel, ClientEarth and Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso brought the case to the Court of Justice of the European Union, questioning the legality of the project's environmental licensing.</p>","fontes":[["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso","https://www.facebook.com/udcovasdobarroso/"],["ClientEarth","https://www.clientearth.org"],["Jornal Mapa","https://www.jornalmapa.pt"]],"stat":"8 years of resistance","link":"https://barrososemminas.org","linkL":"Learn more at barrososemminas.org"},"sophia-beira":{"corpo":"<p>The Sophia (867 MWp) and Beira (269 MWp) projects planned for the municipalities of Fundão, Penamacor and Idanha-a-Nova together cover over 1,158 hectares of montado and classified habitats, putting at risk 231 vertebrate species identified in the environmental impact studies.</p>\n<p>The petition delivered to Parliament asks for the immediate suspension of both licensing processes until an independent, more thorough environmental assessment is carried out.</p>\n<p>The Beira Baixa region concentrates several large-scale projects at once, which environmental organizations flag as a risk of cumulative habitat loss that case-by-case studies fail to capture.</p>","fontes":[["Participação Parlamento","https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5569"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/30/azul/noticia/beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-parlamento-traz-lisboa-oposicao-centrais-solares-2162812"],["SÁBADO","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/de-beira-baixa-a-lisboa-contra-megaprojetos-solares-planeados-para-a-regiao"],["Diário Digital Castelo Branco","https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/70468/plataforma-contra-mega-centrais-solares-na-beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-no-parlamento"],["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/plataforma-contra-mega-centrais-solares-na-beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-no-parlamento_n1707993"]],"stat":"1,158+ ha of montado","link":"https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5569","linkL":"View the initiative in Parliament"},"girabolhos":{"corpo":"<p>The Girabolhos Dam project, on the Mondego River between Seia and Gouveia, has been relaunched to public tender after decades on hold. The Government presents the project as a response to flood risk in the region.</p>\n<p>GEOTA disputes this justification, pointing out that the dam's profile and location would not have contained the water volume responsible for the recent floods used to justify the project.</p>\n<p>The \"Rios Livres\" public petition calls for the project to be reassessed in light of its impact on aquatic wildlife and the natural dynamics of the Mondego River.</p>","fontes":[["GEOTA","https://www.geota.pt"],["Petição Pública: Rios Livres","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=geota-rios-livres"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/ambientalistas-lancam-peticao-contra-construcao-da-barragem-de-girabolhos-no-mondego"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/especial/pais/2026/06/24/em-girabolhos-todo-o-mundo-esta-de-acordo-com-a-barragem-concurso-arranca-a-15-de-julho/475639/"],["Seia Digital","https://seiadigital.pt/2026/07/14/governo-lanca-concurso-para-a-barragem-de-girabolhos-ministra-do-ambiente-anuncia-nova-fase-do-projeto-em-gouveia/"]],"stat":"Tender relaunched","link":"https://www.geota.pt","linkL":"Learn more at geota.pt"},"marao":{"corpo":"<p>The project plans to install around 25,000 photovoltaic panels next to the existing Penedo Ruivo Wind Farm, in Serra do Marão, between 1,120 and 1,220 metres of altitude.</p>\n<p>FAPAS warned of erosion and habitat loss risks in one of the highest-altitude areas of the North region, with direct impact on birds of prey and high-altitude vegetation cover.</p>\n<p>The public petition filed against the project asks for the environmental impact assessment to be reviewed before any final licensing decision.</p>","fontes":[["FAPAS","https://www.fapas.pt/a-fapas-pronuncia-se-contra-a-hibridizacao-fotovoltaica-no-parque-eolico-de-penedo-ruivo-no-marao/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/mobile/pview.aspx?pi=PT130242"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/04/30/azul/noticia/baiao-parecer-desfavoravel-central-fotovoltaica-marao-2173160"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/clima/detalhe/associacao-alerta-para-riscos-de-central-fotovoltaica-no-marao"],["Câmara Municipal de Baião","https://cm-baiao.pt/municipio-de-baiao-emitiu-parecer-sobre-o-projeto-fotovoltaico-de-penedo-ruivo/"]],"stat":"1,120-1,220m altitude","link":"https://www.fapas.pt","linkL":"Learn more at fapas.pt"},"restauro-natureza":{"corpo":"<p>The National Nature Restoration Plan was under public consultation until August 19, 2026, through the Participa Portal. The document sets out an investment of €500 million a year until 2030, spread across 407 measures in eight domains, from rivers and wetlands to forests and marine ecosystems.</p>\n<p>It is the national transposition of the European Nature Restoration Regulation, and the public consultation was the formal moment when anyone could propose changes to the plan before its final version, which Portugal must submit to EU authorities by September 2026.</p>\n<p>Organizations such as ZERO and SPEA submitted technical input during the process. Causas de Raiz will keep following the plan's final version.</p>","fontes":[["Portal Participa","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/projeto-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-e-respetiva-avaliacao-ambiental-estrategica"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-em-consulta-publica-ate-19-de-agosto-500-milhoes-por-ano-e-400-medidas-para-travar-perda-de-biodiversidade/"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/06/02/plano-nacional-preve-quinhentos-milhoes-por-ano-ate-2030-para-restaurar-natureza/472996/"],["ZERO","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/zero-quer-revisao-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-antes-da-entrega-a-bruxelas/"]],"stat":"407 measures · 8 domains","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/projeto-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-e-respetiva-avaliacao-ambiental-estrategica","linkL":"View the plan on the Participa Portal"},"lagoa-salgada":{"corpo":"<p>The Lagoa Salgada mining project, between Grândola and Alcácer do Sal, plans a €196 million investment to mine a polymetallic deposit of copper, lead and zinc near the Alentejo coast.</p>\n<p>The Portuguese Environment Agency has already issued an unfavourable Environmental Impact Statement, citing risks to underground water resources and coastal ecosystems in the region.</p>\n<p>The public petition calls for the definitive cancellation of the licensing process, even in the face of possible appeals from the promoting company.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125518"],["JN","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/protecao-da-agua-justifica-chumbo-da-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente-a-mina-da-lagoa-salgada/18043930"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/01/23/mina-de-cobre-e-zinco-da-lagoa-salgada-volta-a-ter-chumbo-ambiental/"],["Alentejo Ilustrado","https://alentejoilustrado.pt/alcacer-do-sal-muito-feliz-com-chumbo-da-mina-da-lagoa-salgada/"]],"stat":"€196 million","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125518","linkL":"View the petition"},"cultiva":{"corpo":"<p>The Cultiva Project occupies a plot next to Gil Vicente School, in Graça, Lisbon, where a school and community organic garden has run for several years, with regular environmental education activities for children and adults.</p>\n<p>Rizoma Cooperativa Integral, which supports the project, was notified that the space must be vacated by September 12, 2026, as part of planned works on the site.</p>\n<p>The public petition asks for the eviction to be suspended and for a solution that keeps the garden running, given its educational and community value, recognized by the school itself.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=SalvarCultiva"],["Rizoma Cooperativa Integral","https://www.rizomacoop.pt"],["Lisboa Para Pessoas","https://lisboaparapessoas.pt/2026/07/30/horta-cultiva-rizoma-gil-vicente-exercito/"]],"stat":"Eviction on Sept 12, 2026","link":"https://www.rizomacoop.pt","linkL":"Learn more at rizomacoop.pt"},"praias-arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>Since July 2025, a lawsuit (case 4833/25.7T8STB) has been running in the Judicial Court of Setúbal, filed by Palácio da Comenda, S.A., current holder of the Quinta Herdade da Comenda estate, against the Portuguese State and the Portuguese Environment Agency. The company claims private ownership of five beaches, a municipal road and the Comenda picnic park: the beaches of Rasca, Comenda, Rainha, Maria Esguelha and Albarquel.</p>\n<p>The \"Deslarrrguem a Arrábida!\" movement brought together hundreds of people for a march between Setúbal and the Comenda Recreation Park, in protest against the attempted private appropriation and against restrictions on public access to the area.</p>\n<p>The petition delivered to Parliament has passed 12,500 signatures and will be debated in Parliament. The Government and Setúbal City Council have publicly reaffirmed that the beaches are public, trusting the courts to stop the process.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/19/centenas-de-pessoas-marcham-em-setubal-contra-privatizacao-de-praias-e-acessos-da-arrabida/"],["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/uma-multidao-juntou-se-na-caminhada-para-gritar-deslarrrguem-arrabida/98408"],["SAPO Notícias","https://sapo.pt/artigo/arrabida-governo-reafirma-que-praias-sao-publicas-e-camara-de-setubal-confia-na-justica-para-travar-privatizacao-6a592bb5bbff543e35398909"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/pt/Centenas-protestam-contra-a-privatiza%C3%A7%C3%A3o-das-praias-de-Arr%C3%A1bida--enquanto-a-pol%C3%AAmica-sobre-o-acesso-p%C3%BAblico-se-intensifica./"],["ADN Agência de Notícias","https://www.adn-agenciadenoticias.com/2026/06/herdade-da-comenda-reclama-cinco-praias.html"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/nacional/centenas-marcham-em-defesa-de-cinco-praias-e-dos-acessos-da-arrabida/"],["Público: parliamentary debate","https://publico.pt/2026/06/26/local/noticia/peticao-vai-conseguir-privatizacao-praias-arrabida-debatida-parlamento-2179605"],["PT Green: 12,500 signatures","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/peticao-com-mais-de-12-500-assinaturas-pede-debate-parlamentar-sobre-alegada-privatizacao-de-cinco-praias-de-setubal/"]],"stat":"12,500+ signatures","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/19/centenas-de-pessoas-marcham-em-setubal-contra-privatizacao-de-praias-e-acessos-da-arrabida/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"costa-terra-melides":{"corpo":"<p>Between Tróia and Melides, in the municipality of Grândola, the luxury resort Costa Terra occupies an estate of around 850 hectares along the coast, developed by Discovery Land Company through CostaTerra, Sociedade Imobiliária de Grândola. Private security, fencing and ID checks restrict access to public beaches in the area, including Galé-Fontainhas beach, where for years visitors had to hand over their ID card at the entrance to a former campsite the company had acquired.</p>\n<p>In July 2025, an inspection by the Portuguese Environment Agency, ordered by the Government, identified seven beaches in Grândola municipality with access conditioned by tourism developments: Camarinhas, Galé-Fontaínhas and Tróia-Galé already operating, and Duna Cinzenta, Golfinhos, Garças and Pinheirinho still under construction. The Government promised signage, new parking and public access corridors.</p>\n<p>A year later, in August 2026, an investigative report again found unresolved physical barriers, particularly at Galé-Fontainhas and Aberta Nova beaches. Quercus publicly accused the Minister of Environment and the Environment Agency of \"throwing sand in the eyes\" of the Portuguese public, noting that a letter sent in June 2026 had never received a reply, and warned of the environmental cost of these developments: water scarcity, destruction of dune systems and disregard for coastal planning rules.</p>\n<p>The Dunas Livres Association, founded in 2020 by biologists, a forestry engineer and an architect, has for years documented private security photographing visitors and licence plates near Costa Terra. After months without a response to requests for public documents about the development, the association took the case to the Administrative Court of Beja, which ruled in its favour against Grândola council. Along the 45 kilometres of coast between Tróia and Melides, a survey by Expresso found limited or non-existent access along about 80% of the shoreline, with beach umbrella rentals reaching €200 a day on the most sought-after beaches.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus — statement, 10 Aug 2026","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/10/quercus-exige-explicacoes-a-ministra-do-ambiente-e-ao-presidente-da-cm-de-grandola-sobre-barreiras-e-controlo-de-acessos-em-praias-de-melides/"],["Observador — APA inspection","https://observador.pt/2025/07/09/grandola-inspecao-detetou-acesso-condicionado-a-sete-praias-por-empreendimentos-a-operar-ou-em-construcao/"],["Público — seven beaches with conditioned access","https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/09/local/noticia/maioria-praias-grandola-lei-cumprida-ha-irregularidades-2139630"],["ECO — the millionaire revolution on the Alentejo coast","https://eco.sapo.pt/especiais/revolucao-milionaria-no-litoral-alentejano-construcao-toma-conta-dos-45-km-de-troia-a-melides/"],["Postal — the beach that costs €42","https://postal.pt/nacional/conheca-a-praia-a-sul-de-lisboa-cujo-acesso-custa-42e-e-onde-uma-sombra-pode-chegar-aos-200e/"],["TSF — minister promises to resolve Galé-Fontainhas","https://www.tsf.pt/sociedade/artigo/condicionamento-ao-acesso-a-praia-da-gale-fontainhas-vai-ser-resolvido-nao-esta-de-acordo-com-espirito-de-praia-publica/18114955"],["Tal&Qual — Mexican CostaTerra owners denounced in Europe","https://talequal.pt/mexicanos-do-costaterra-denunciados-na-europa/"],["LPN — petition for the Tróia Peninsula","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/cidadania/campanhas/pela-preservacao-do-patrimonio-natural-da-peninsula-de-troia"]],"stat":"7 beaches with conditioned access in Grândola","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/10/quercus-exige-explicacoes-a-ministra-do-ambiente-e-ao-presidente-da-cm-de-grandola-sobre-barreiras-e-controlo-de-acessos-em-praias-de-melides/","linkL":"Read the Quercus statement"},"verdelago-castro-marim":{"corpo":"<p>Between August and September 2025, the Portuguese Environment Agency inspected 29 licensed beaches in the Algarve in municipalities \"where there were reports of irregularities or a history of incidents\". In Castro Marim, the inspection confirmed that access to Verdelago beach runs through the interior of a tourism development, via a gate with a buzzer and unclear signage about the public route.</p>\n<p>As a corrective measure, the Agency notified the developer to install clear signage indicating the public access route to the beach and to create alternative parking to the west, closer to the sand, removing the dependence on the conditioned entrance through the development.</p>\n<p>The Agency's president, José Pimenta Machado, confirmed that around ten violation notices were issued in this inspection and that offenders have been or will be notified. He noted that concessions \"are licensed to occupy a given space\" and that public beach access must be guaranteed regardless of neighboring tourism developments.</p>\n<p>The Verdelago case is not isolated in the Algarve: in the same inspection, Poço Velho beach, in Albufeira, was found with its main access completely blocked by a gate on private land.</p>","fontes":[["Postal — APA inspection","https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/"],["Observador — rescue posts used as storage","https://observador.pt/2025/10/27/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-diz-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/pt/noticias/2025-10-29/irregularidades-detectadas-nas-praias-algarvias/908678"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2025/10/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-e-sanitarios-encerrados/"]],"stat":"29 beaches inspected · conditioned access confirmed at Verdelago","link":"https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/","linkL":"Read on Postal"},"poco-velho-aveiros-albufeira":{"corpo":"<p>Between August and September 2025, the Portuguese Environment Agency inspected 29 licensed beaches in the Algarve in municipalities \"where there were reports of irregularities or a history of incidents\". In Albufeira, the inspection confirmed that the main access to Poço Velho beach is closed by a gate on private land, with no regularized parking nearby. The Agency is now identifying and contacting the landowners, aiming to reopen the gate and coordinate parking and access planning with the municipal council.</p>\n<p>The Poço Velho case is not isolated in the municipality. In 2014, Praia dos Aveiros, in the same area, had its access blocked by a gate after a tourism developer claimed ownership of the access path in court. The Albufeira court eventually ordered the municipal council to restore the public signage, but the dispute left a precedent for how easily a private developer can, in practice, condition access to a legally public beach.</p>\n<p>The 2025 inspection also found other irregularities linked to beach concessions in the Algarve: at Monte Gordo, bathroom facilities closed or restricted to concession clients, despite access to bathrooms being universal by law; and occupation of the sand beyond the licensed area at Armação de Pêra and at Portimão beaches such as Rocha, Alvor and Prainha.</p>\n<p>The Agency's president, José Pimenta Machado, confirmed that around ten violation notices were issued in this inspection and that offenders have been or will be notified.</p>","fontes":[["Postal — APA inspection","https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/"],["Observador — rescue posts used as storage","https://observador.pt/2025/10/27/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-diz-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/pt/noticias/2025-10-29/irregularidades-detectadas-nas-praias-algarvias/908678"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2025/10/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-e-sanitarios-encerrados/"],["Público (2014) — Praia dos Aveiros","https://www.publico.pt/2014/06/11/local/noticia/praia-dos-aveiros-em-albufeira-vai-ter-cancela-a-barrar-o-acesso-ao-mar-1639295"],["oturismo.pt (2014) — Praia dos Aveiros","https://www.oturismo.pt/oturismo/26181-praia-dos-aveiros-passou-de-publica-a-privada-por-inercia-da-autarquia-de-albufeira.html"]],"stat":"29 beaches inspected · access blocked at Poço Velho since at least 2025, precedent at Aveiros since 2014","link":"https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/","linkL":"Read on Postal"},"borba":{"corpo":"<p>The Borba and Vila Viçosa region has 232 registered marble quarries, one of the highest densities of mining activity in the country.</p>\n<p>Independent surveys point out that over half of these quarries operate with no valid environmental recovery plan, in breach of legislation on landscape recovery of mined areas.</p>\n<p>The lack of regular inspection has been identified as the main obstacle to correcting this situation, leaving degraded areas without a recovery plan even after mining has ended.</p>","fontes":[["SÁBADO","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/borba-ambientalistas-apontam-centenas-de-pedreiras-abandonadas-sem-salvaguardas-ambientais"],["SAPO 24","https://24.sapo.pt/atualidade/artigos/acidenteborba-ambientalistas-apontam-centenas-de-pedreiras-abandonadas-sem-salvaguardas-ambientais"],["Linhas de Elvas","https://linhasdeelvas.pt/2026/07/15/secretario-de-estado-adjunto-e-da-energia-reuniu-com-municipio-de-vila-vicosa-para-analisar-plano-de-intervencao-nas-pedreiras/"]],"stat":"232 registered quarries","link":"","linkL":""},"arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>Secil has operated limestone quarries within the boundaries of Arrábida Natural Park for decades, in an area classified as of high ecological and landscape value.</p>\n<p>Seven environmental organizations, including LPN, formally demanded that the company present a decommissioning and landscape recovery plan for the areas already mined, with a defined timeline.</p>\n<p>Secil has not publicly responded with a concrete timeline to date, and mining continues within the protected area.</p>","fontes":[["LPN","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/lpn-pede-plano-de-desativacao-das-pedreiras-da-secil-no-parque-natural-da-arrabida"],["TSF","https://www.tsf.pt/portugal/sociedade/ambientalistas-pedem-secil-plano-de-desativacao-de-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida-16729282.html"],["GreenSavers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/ambientalistas-exigem-o-fim-definitivo-das-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida/"],["Setúbal Mais","https://setubalmais.pt/ccdr-chumba-ampliacao-da-pedreira-da-secil-na-arrabida/"]],"stat":"7 organizations","link":"","linkL":""},"incendios":{"corpo":"<p>By 19 August 2026, Portugal had recorded 6,666 rural fires and 63,347 hectares of burned area, according to the Integrated Rural Fire Management System (SGIFR), run by AGIF. It is the fifth worst year for burned area in the decade, behind 2017, 2025, 2016 and 2022, and the sixth worst year for number of fires, reversing the downward trend seen since 2022.</p>\n<p>The fire that broke out in Tourelhe, Vouzela, on 2 July officially became Europe's largest wildfire of 2026, alone accounting for around 70% of all area burned in Portugal this year, with the destruction nearly quadrupling compared to the equivalent 2025 fire. According to Diário de Notícias, this is already the worst cumulative record since the tragic year of 2017 and the Pedrógão Grande fire.</p>\n<p>Since 15 August, several significant fires have broken out daily, mostly in the north, most notably in Torre de Moncorvo, Bragança district, the longest-running and still active. The municipalities with the most burned area in 2026 are Valpaços, Mirandela, Águeda and Vouzela. In July, a firefighter was injured while fighting the Santo Tirso fire and was taken to Hospital do Médio Ave.</p>\n<p>Agricultural burning was the leading cause of fires recorded up to 15 August, responsible for 37% of incidents. By region, the North has the most burned area (34,929 ha), followed by the Centre (20,452 ha) and the Alentejo (3,335 ha).</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias — European record","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/vouzela-atira-portugal-para-recorde-da-europa-de-rea-ardida-em-2026"],["ECO — burned area four times smaller, but more fires","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/08/18/area-ardida-quatro-vezes-menor-este-ano-mas-numero-de-fogos-aumenta/"],["CNN Portugal — agricultural burning behind most fires","https://cnnportugal.iol.pt/incendios/fogos/incendios-queimas-e-queimadas-na-origem-da-maior-parte-dos-fogos-ate-15-de-agosto/20260819/6a858fa0d34ed0733ba8089b"],["Diário de Coimbra","https://www.diariocoimbra.pt/2026/08/19/queimas-sao-principal-causa-dos-incendios-em-portugal-ate-15-de-agosto/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/06/area-ardida-duplicou-em-cinco-dias-e-ja-e-a-maior-desde-2017-mais-de-15-000-hectares-queimados-entre-1-e-5-de-julho/"]],"stat":"63,347 hectares burned · Vouzela fire is Europe's largest of 2026","link":"https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/vouzela-atira-portugal-para-recorde-da-europa-de-rea-ardida-em-2026","linkL":"Read on Diário de Notícias"},"castelo-bode":{"corpo":"<p>The Amara Village development plans a 50-hectare tourist resort on the shores of the Castelo de Bode reservoir, in Tomar, the country's second-largest freshwater reserve.</p>\n<p>The licensing process moved forward with no Environmental Impact Assessment, despite the scale of the project and its location next to one of the main water supply reserves for the Centre region.</p>\n<p>Local environmental associations and Quercus question the legality of the process, asking for it to be suspended until a full environmental assessment is carried out.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/07/quercus-considera-escandaloso-avanco-de-projeto-turistico-na-albufeira-de-castelo-de-bode-sem-avaliacao-de-impacte-ambiental/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/07/quercus-contesta-avanco-de-aldeamento-turistico-de-luxo-em-tomar-sem-avaliacao-ambiental/"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/quercus-contesta-avanco-de-aldeamento-turistico-de-luxo-em-tomar-sem-avaliacao-ambiental/"],["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/sociedade/2026-07-18-turismo-de-luxo-na-albufeira-de-castelo-de-bode-levanta-preocupacoes-880d34a9"]],"stat":"50 hectares","link":"","linkL":""},"sobreira":{"corpo":"<p>EDP is preparing, in Pedrógão, in the municipality of Vidigueira, its largest photovoltaic plant in Europe, with construction planned to start in November 2026.</p>\n<p>The project's environmental impact study classifies the impacts on Bonelli's eagle, a threatened species with confirmed presence in the region, and on several protected bat species, as \"very significant\".</p>\n<p>Environmental organizations are asking for the project layout to be revised to preserve flight corridors and hunting areas essential to these species' survival in the region.</p>","fontes":[["LPN","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-central-fotovoltaica-da-sobreira-de-baixo-"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/11/25/vai-nascer-no-alentejo-a-maior-central-fotovoltaica-da-edp-na-europa/"],["Jornal Económico","https://leitor.jornaleconomico.pt/noticia/edp-com-projeto-para-instalar-a-sua-maior-central-solar-europeia-no-alentejo"],["Câmara Municipal de Vidigueira","https://cm-vidigueira.pt/31331/consulta-publica--central-fotovoltaica-da-sobreira-de-baixo"]],"stat":"EDP's largest plant in Europe","link":"","linkL":""},"apa-icnf":{"corpo":"<p>The ongoing reform at the Portuguese Environment Agency and the Institute for Nature Conservation and Forests changes the environmental licensing model, replacing mandatory prior assessment with after-the-fact inspection for several project categories.</p>\n<p>The Government justifies the change as part of an \"administrative simplification\" package, cutting timelines and documentation requirements for project developers.</p>\n<p>SPEA and other environmental organizations warn that after-the-fact inspection typically comes too late to prevent irreversible damage to sensitive ecosystems, reversing the precautionary principle in environmental protection.</p>","fontes":[["SPEA","https://spea.pt/reforma-da-apa-e-do-icnf-reestruturar-sim-desproteger-nunca/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/07/azul/noticia/ambientalistas-querem-reforma-apa-icnf-traga-capacidade-qualidade-tecnica-2173882"],["Wilder","https://wilder.pt/historias/icnf-e-apa-zero-spea-e-quercus-questionam-reestruturacao-anunciada-pela-ministra-do-ambiente"],["e24","https://e24.pt/spea-reforma-apa-icnf-desproteger-natureza/"]],"stat":"National reform","link":"","linkL":""},"emergencia-climatica":{"corpo":"<p>More than 100 Portuguese municipalities still haven't submitted the municipal climate action plans required by law, leaving the country without a coordinated territorial response to the climate emergency.</p>\n<p>The absence of these plans limits local capacity to respond to extreme events, from heatwaves to floods, which are becoming more frequent and more intense.</p>\n<p>Organizations such as ZERO are asking the Government for binding deadlines and technical support for municipalities with fewer resources to meet this legal obligation.</p>","fontes":[["ZERO","https://zero.ong/noticias/zero-entende-que-planos-municipais-e-regionais-de-acao-climatica-sao-parte-da-resposta-as-ondas-de-calor-e-aos-incendios-rurais-mas-importa-elabora-los/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2025/02/01/azul/noticia/portugal-declarou-emergencia-climatica-ha-tres-anos-faltou-urgencia-politica-2120885"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/mais-de-metade-dos-municipios-portugueses-ainda-nao-tem-um-plano-municipal-de-acao-climatica-diz-estudo"]],"stat":"100+ municipalities missing plans","link":"","linkL":""},"montijo-alcochete":{"corpo":"<p>After the Montijo airport project was stopped on environmental grounds, the Government chose the Alcochete firing range as the new site for Lisbon's future airport.</p>\n<p>The new location carries even greater environmental risks: construction threatens over 250,000 cork oaks and overlaps with the Tejo-Sado aquifer, the country's largest underground freshwater reserve.</p>\n<p>Environmental organizations and local associations are calling for a full strategic environmental assessment before any final decision, warning that the impacts may be even more severe than those of the original Montijo project.</p>","fontes":[["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/05/14/azul/noticia/alcochete-opcao-problematica-novo-aeroporto-ambientalistas-2090439"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/24/aeroporto-ambientalistas-avisam-que-ha-riscos-para-o-aquifero-e-para-abastecimento-de-agua-a-setubal/"],["O Setubalense","https://osetubalense.com/ultimas/quercus-diz-que-futuro-aeroporto-poe-em-risco-aquifero-e-abastecimento-de-agua"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/new-lisbon-airport-will-need-to-divert-water-courses/"]],"stat":"250,000+ cork oaks threatened","link":"","linkL":""},"valtreixal":{"corpo":"<p>The Valtreixal mining project, in Calabor, in the Spanish province of Zamora, planned an open-pit operation a few kilometres from the Portuguese border, next to Montesinho Natural Park.</p>\n<p>Movimento UIVO, created in 2021 by residents on both sides of the border, mobilized against the project, warning of contamination risk to watercourses shared between Portugal and Spain.</p>\n<p>The regional government of Castile and León refused the project's environmental permit, a result the movement considers significant for the whole cross-border region, while it remains alert to possible appeals from the developer.</p>","fontes":[["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/incongruencias-do-estudo-de-impacto-ambiental-da-mina-em-calabor-preocupam-movimento-uivo"],["Notícias ao Minuto","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/2994018/espanha-trava-mina-perto-de-braganca-e-do-parque-de-montesinho"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/05/24/junta-de-castela-e-leao-trava-exploracao-mineira-junto-a-fronteira-de-braganca/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/junta-de-castela-e-leao-impede-exploracao-mineira-em-calabor-a-5-km-de-braganca"],["eldiario.es (Espanha)","https://www.eldiario.es/castilla-y-leon/castilla-leon-niega-licencia-ambiental-mina-wolframio-fronteriza-levanto-fuerte-rechazo-portugal_1_13218822.html"]],"stat":"Permit refused","link":"https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/incongruencias-do-estudo-de-impacto-ambiental-da-mina-em-calabor-preocupam-movimento-uivo","linkL":"Read on esquerda.net"},"pszaer":{"corpo":"<p>ZAER — Renewable Energy Acceleration Zones — stem from the EU's RED III directive and exempt solar and wind projects located within them from individual Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA). The exemption rests on a strategic environmental assessment carried out in bulk, for the whole zone, before any actual project exists.</p>\n<p>The \"Green Map\" of candidate zones, under the Sectoral Programme for ZAER (PSZAER), was in public consultation between 17 June and 15 July 2026, with 1,302 zones mapped — 792 for solar and 510 for wind, corresponding to roughly 371,000 hectares for solar and 84,000 for wind.</p>\n<p>Quercus issued an unfavourable opinion on the last day of the consultation, calling the programme a \"Black Desert\": according to the association, the proposal covered around 7% of mainland territory — more than the country's entire urban footprint — when 1% would suffice to meet solar targets, with maps supplied at a scale useless for serious analysis (1:3,500,000) and without open geographic files. Plataforma Nordeste Vivo, in Northeast Trás-os-Montes, also contests the overlap of several zones with priority conservation areas.</p>\n<p>After the consultation, the Government announced the pre-approval of more than 800 zones (500 for solar, 300 for wind) in about 170 municipalities, now saying this corresponds to roughly 1% of mainland territory, and guaranteed municipalities \"full autonomy\" to decide where these zones sit within their boundaries. Integration into municipal master plans (PDM) should happen between 2026 and 2028 — but the exemption from individual EIA remains the core change, and it is what Causas de Raiz keeps monitoring.</p>","fontes":[["SAPO — pre-approval of over 800 ZAER zones","https://sapo.pt/artigo/governo-anuncia-pre-aprovacao-de-mais-de-800-areas-de-aceleracao-de-energias-renovaveis-6a87370cd0cbd78bc72e9fee"],["RTP — \"Black Desert\": Quercus issues unfavourable opinion on PSZAER","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/deserto-negro-quercus-da-parecer-desfavoravel-ao-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-das-energias-renovaveis_a1753539"],["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/15/quercus-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-ao-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-das-energias-renovaveis/"],["Observador — \"full autonomy\" for municipalities","https://observador.pt/2026/07/16/governo-garante-total-autonomia-dos-municipios-na-definicao-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["Ambiente Online — public consultation ends amid criticism","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/programa-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis-termina-consulta-publica-sob-criticas-de-quercus-e-municipios"],["Macedo Vitorino — legal note on ZAER","https://www.macedovitorino.com/conhecimento/insights/Governo-coloca-as-ZAER-em-consulta/6960/"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/23/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos/"]],"stat":"800+ ZAER zones · ~170 municipalities · ~1% of territory","link":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/governo-anuncia-pre-aprovacao-de-mais-de-800-areas-de-aceleracao-de-energias-renovaveis-6a87370cd0cbd78bc72e9fee","linkL":"Read on SAPO"},"monte-rei":{"corpo":"<p>The Monte Rei resort, in Vila Nova de Cacela, wants to build a second 56-hectare golf course, in an Algarve region that has faced critical water scarcity for several consecutive years.</p>\n<p>ZERO called the project \"incompatible with the water emergency\" the region faces, questioning the priority given to water use for recreational purposes over the water supply needs of local residents.</p>\n<p>The licensing process received an unfavourable opinion, but the developer keeps the project under review, with the possibility of appealing the decision.</p>","fontes":[["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2024/02/novo-campo-de-golfe-no-algarve-e-projeto-incompativel-com-a-emergencia-hidrica-que-se-vive/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/02/01/local/noticia/seca-campo-golfe-algarve-apa-impoe-rega-aguas-residuais-2078793"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/nacional/novo-campo-de-golfe-em-vila-real-de-santo-antonio-so-avanca-se-rega-for-com-agua-tratada/"]],"stat":"56 hectares","link":"","linkL":""},"serta":{"corpo":"<p>Over 25% of the Sertã municipality's area is identified in the national plan as a solar acceleration zone, one of the highest proportions in the country.</p>\n<p>Sertã City Council, joined by neighbouring municipalities in Beira Baixa, issued an unfavourable opinion on the programme, warning of the cumulative impact on the landscape, agriculture and municipal land-use planning.</p>\n<p>The regional pushback reflects a broader concern about the disproportionate concentration of large-scale energy projects in inland territories, with no equivalent compensation for local communities.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/14/camara-da-serta-da-parecer-desfavoravel-as-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["Notícias de Coimbra","https://www.noticiasdecoimbra.pt/camara-da-serta-da-parecer-desfavoravel-as-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/serta-emite-parecer-negativo-a-zona-de-aceleracao-para-as-energias-renovaveis/"],["Mais Beiras","https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/serta-municipio-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-a-proposta-do-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-para-as-energias-renovaveis"]],"stat":"25%+ of the municipality","link":"","linkL":""},"ia-sines":{"corpo":"<p>The announcement of an artificial intelligence gigafactory in Sines is presented as a milestone of \"technological sovereignty\" for the country, but the project carries energy and water needs that are rarely discussed in public.</p>\n<p>Water supply is planned through desalinated seawater, a process that has already triggered a legal dispute over the terms of the concession. The data centre's energy consumption will require building Europe's largest solar plant in the region, involving forest felling in areas that are currently classified.</p>\n<p>Local organizations from the Alentejo coast, including TAMLA, question the real environmental cost of a project presented mainly in economic and geopolitical terms.</p>","fontes":[["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/06/17/azul/noticia/edp-guerra-juridica-estado-garantir-agua-mar-sines-2178488"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/especiais/edp-abre-batalha-juridica-com-o-estado-pelo-fornecimento-da-agua-do-mar-em-sines/"],["Jornal de Negócios","https://www.jornaldenegocios.pt/economia/ambiente/detalhe/aguas-de-portugal-da-primeiro-passo-para-a-dessalinizadora-de-sines-prevista-para-2031"],["Sul Informação","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2023/10/movimentos-protestam-em-sines-e-pedem-travao-na-destruicao-do-litoral-alentejano/"]],"stat":"Europe's largest solar plant","link":"","linkL":""},"curral-freiras":{"corpo":"<p>The cable car and adventure park project in Curral das Freiras, Câmara de Lobos, was approved despite being located in a known nesting area of Zino's petrel, one of the world's most endangered seabirds, endemic to Madeira.</p>\n<p>Quercus-Madeira formally challenged the decision, warning that the environmental impact study fails to robustly rule out risk to the species, which is critically endangered.</p>\n<p>The Ecologist Party, Os Verdes, with a structure in Madeira, reiterated to the regional ICNF its firm opposition to the project, asking for the licensing decision to be reviewed.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://sapo.pt/artigo/quercus-da-madeira-contra-o-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras-6a18a717795ed400b3851124"],["Os Verdes","https://osverdes.pt/acao-ecologista/eleicoes/sobre-o-sistema-de-telefericos-do-curral-das-freiras/"],["DNoticias","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2026/5/28/493614-quercus-da-madeira-contra-o-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras/"],["JM Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/ver/167333/Os_Verdes_reiteram_posicao_contra_projeto_de_teleferico_no_Curral_das_Freiras"],["Funchal Notícias","https://funchalnoticias.net/2026/07/02/quercus-madeira-impugna-decisao-de-conformidade-ambiental-do-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras/"]],"stat":"Critically endangered species","link":"","linkL":""},"lagoas-acores":{"corpo":"<p>Lagoa das Furnas and Lagoa das Sete Cidades, two of São Miguel Island's landscape landmarks, face a growing eutrophication process, linked to the intensification of dairy production in the surrounding watersheds.</p>\n<p>Excess fertilizer and animal waste run off into the lakes, feeding algae blooms that reduce the oxygen available in the water and threaten local aquatic ecosystems.</p>\n<p>The problem is structural: it requires changes in farming practices across the whole watershed, not just isolated measures at the lakes themselves, and involves balancing an economic activity central to the Azores with the preservation of two of its most emblematic landscapes.</p>","fontes":[["Açoriano Oriental","https://www.acorianooriental.pt/noticia/regiao-destaca-esforco-no-combate-a-eutrofizacao-nas-lagoas-294433"],["Diário de Notícias","https://www.dn.pt/lusa/governo-dos-acores-destaca-esforco-no-combate-a-eutrofizacao-nas-lagoas-10179507.html"]],"stat":"Two lakes affected","link":"","linkL":""},"lagoa-salgados-silves":{"corpo":"<p>Lagoa dos Salgados, between Armação de Pêra and Albufeira, is the last stretch of the Algarve coast with no ecological protection status at all. On November 22, 2025, the Institute for Nature Conservation and Forests made public a proposal to classify a 400-hectare Natural Reserve at the site, after more than 20 years of requests from environmental organizations.</p>\n<p>The proposal directly conflicts with the Praia Grande Eco-Resort tourism project, which plans an investment of around €200 million in three hotels, two villages, an 18-hole golf course and over two kilometres of beachfront, totalling 4,000 beds. Silves's new Municipal Master Plan already excludes the resort from the Praia Grande area, next to the lagoon.</p>\n<p>On July 28, 2026, Silves City Council met with the State Secretary for the Environment to reiterate the need to move forward with the classification process. The Movimento Participativo Lagoa dos Salgados brings together nine organizations, Almargem, A Rocha, ANP|WWF, Vita Nativa, LPN, Quercus-ANCN, Sociedade Portuguesa de Botânica, SPEA and ZERO, in a campaign that has gathered over 35,000 signatures over the years through the \"Save Salgados\" petition.</p>","fontes":[["Algarve Marafado","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/07/30/avanca-processo-para-a-criacao-de-nova-reserva-natural-no-algarve/"],["LPN","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/projeto-ressuscitado-ameaca-futura-reserva-natural-da-lagoa-dos-salgados-"],["SPEA","https://spea.pt/imprensa/projeto-ressuscitado-ameaca-futura-reserva-natural-da-lagoa-dos-salgados/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/novo-plano-diretor-municipal-de-silves-ja-exclui-resort-junto-a-lagoa-dos-salgados"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2021/12/04/local/noticia/lagoa-salgados-passa-reserva-natural-poe-causa-4-mil-camas-ali-previstas-1987407"]],"stat":"400 hectares proposed","link":"https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/07/30/avanca-processo-para-a-criacao-de-nova-reserva-natural-no-algarve/","linkL":"Read on Algarve Marafado"},"nordeste-vivo-mogadouro":{"corpo":"<p>At the first public information session on renewable energy megaprojects in Northeast Trás-os-Montes, held in Mogadouro with around 50 people present, Plataforma Nordeste Vivo confirmed that most residents did not know the real scale of the projects already built or approved. According to José Jambas, one of the movement's founders, the continuous stretch of solar panels already exceeds 1,500 hectares across the Planalto Mirandês.</p>\n<p>In Miranda do Douro, the hybridization project promoted by Engie plans to install 35 wind turbines 200 metres tall, more than half the height of the Eiffel Tower. The developers' own environmental impact studies show that hundreds of hectares of farmland, including dryland crops, will go uncultivated for the 30-year lifespan of the projects.</p>\n<p>Plataforma Nordeste Vivo said it would move forward with legal injunctions and new complaints to the Public Prosecutor's Office. The movement is not opposed to renewable energy itself, but argues that rooftops, industrial zones, parking lots and other existing infrastructure should be used first, before farmland and forest land.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/12/azul/noticia/engie-avanca-hibridizacao-hidroelectricas-transmontanas-energia-fotovoltaica-2174366"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/15/plataforma-nordeste-vivo-exige-suspensao-do-programa-de-renovaveis-e-acusa-governo-de-conduzir-processo-na-sombra/"],["Mensageiro de Bragança","https://www.mdb.pt/index.php/noticia/plataforma-nordeste-vivo-exige-suspensao-do-pszaer-pedindo-responsabilidade-politica-0"],["Jornal Nordeste: council opposition","https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/presidente-da-camara-de-mogadouro-reforca-oposicao-a-novos-parques-renovaveis"],["Petição Pública: Travanca","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT131073"]],"stat":"1,500+ hectares already covered","link":"https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos","linkL":"Read on Jornal Nordeste"},"eolico-mira-odemira":{"corpo":"<p>Galp submitted to the Portuguese Environment Agency a scope-definition proposal for the \"Mira Wind Project\", a hybrid wind-solar plant with around 22 turbines and about 158 megawatts of capacity, spanning the municipalities of Odemira and Ourique.</p>\n<p>Residents of the parishes of Relíquias, São Martinho das Amoreiras, Luzianes-Gare and Santa Clara-a-Velha express total rejection of the project. This is already Galp's second project in the region, after the Cachenas wind farm, next to its green hydrogen unit in Sines, was abandoned in 2026 following an unfavourable opinion and a petition with over 5,595 signatures.</p>\n<p>The current petition asks Odemira City Council and the competent authorities to stop the new project before it advances to the next stage of environmental licensing.</p>","fontes":[["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/projeto-eolico-do-mira-galp-planeia-novo-projeto-hibrido-eolico-solar-nos-concelhos-de-odemira-e-ourique/"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/22/galp-estuda-projeto-eolico-com-cerca-de-22-aerogeradores-entre-ourique-e-odemira/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/01/27/parque-eolico-com-mega-aerogeradores-para-milfontes-suscita-oposicao-expressiva-e-galp-tera-de-fundamentar-e-detalhar-proposta/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT131724"]],"stat":"2,159+ signatures","link":"https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/projeto-eolico-do-mira-galp-planeia-novo-projeto-hibrido-eolico-solar-nos-concelhos-de-odemira-e-ourique/","linkL":"Read on Sul Informação"},"biometano-torres-novas":{"corpo":"<p>Gasdaterra plans to build a biomethane production unit in Árgea, in the municipality of Torres Novas, with an estimated investment of 18 million euros, to treat around 98,000 tonnes of waste a year and produce 6.5 million cubic metres of biomethane.</p>\n<p>Residents, backed by the Residents Commission, are contesting the site, just a few hundred metres from the village, over heavy traffic, air emissions, the risk of bad odours and well contamination. Torres Novas Municipal Assembly united against the project, and the Residents Commission called a protest vigil.</p>\n<p>The public consultation ran until 3 July 2026 on the Participa portal, but residents are asking for a further in-person public session and an unfavourable opinion from the Portuguese Environment Agency on the proposed site.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/politica/2026-05-27-central-de-biometano-projectada-para-torres-novas-gera-contestacao-e-preocupa-autarcas-316867ff"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/assembleia-municipal-de-torres-novas-une-se-contra-unidade-de-biometano-em-argea/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/17/comissao-de-utentes-convoca-vigilia-contra-unidade-de-biometano-em-torres-novas/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/contestacao-a-unidade-de-biometano-em-torres-novas-ganha-forca-com-apoio-de-moradores-e-autarcas"]],"stat":"2,798+ signatures","link":"https://omirante.pt/politica/2026-05-27-central-de-biometano-projectada-para-torres-novas-gera-contestacao-e-preocupa-autarcas-316867ff","linkL":"Read on O Mirante"},"mina-adagoi":{"corpo":"<p>The C-192 Adagoi mining concession, located in the parishes of Capeludos and Bragado, in Vila Pouca de Aguiar, plans to mine quartz, feldspar and lithium through the company MCS, which describes the project as \"relatively small-scale and low-impact\".</p>\n<p>Citizens concerned with protecting the environment, public health and sustainable development are asking for clarification on the impacts on water resources, soils, biodiversity and the local landscape, as well as on the financial guarantees planned for environmental recovery.</p>\n<p>The project adds to other concessions in the same Barroso region, where mining pressure on farming communities has already been a source of resistance for several years.</p>","fontes":[["A Voz de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.avozdetrasosmontes.pt/projeto-de-exploracao-mineira-da-origem-a-peticao/"],["Jornal de Chaves","https://jornaldechaves.pt/noticia?id=11310"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/02/23/mcs-quer-explorar-feldspato-em-vila-pouca-de-aguiar-mas-enfrenta-oposicao/"]],"stat":"536+ signatures","link":"https://www.avozdetrasosmontes.pt/projeto-de-exploracao-mineira-da-origem-a-peticao/","linkL":"Read on A Voz de Trás-os-Montes"},"sao-luis-odemira":{"corpo":"<p>The Juntos por São Luís movement is raising the alarm over a mega photovoltaic plant planned for the Poldreiros do Meio and Lameiros area, in the parish of São Luís, municipality of Odemira, covering between 100 and 150 hectares inside the Natura 2000 network, in National Ecological Reserve areas.</p>\n<p>Juntos por São Luís is part of the Movimento Energia Justa e Sustentável (MEJS), a national platform created by nine civic movements and associations against the spread of solar and wind megaprojects \"with unacceptable location and scale\", defending a just energy transition.</p>\n<p>The petition calls for the project's site to be reviewed and for already artificial land, such as rooftops and industrial zones, to be prioritised before farmland and forest land.</p>","fontes":[["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos_n1745481"],["Sul Informação","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2026/06/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos"],["Jornal Económico","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos/"]],"stat":"700+ signatures","link":"https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos_n1745481","linkL":"Read on RTP"},"pellets-cercal-alentejo":{"corpo":"<p>A fire at the pellet factory in the Cercal do Alentejo Business Zone began on 21 July, starting in a silo that burst, spreading to wood stored outside and to a neighbouring rural area. It was only brought under control ten days later, on 31 July.</p>\n<p>The Juntos pelo Cercal civic movement says residents were exposed to toxic smoke for more than two weeks, with complaints of respiratory problems and eye irritation, and warns that the village's proximity to the factory leaves the community \"always exposed to harmful factors\" from the industrial zone.</p>\n<p>The movement is demanding the immediate suspension of the factory under current conditions, an independent environmental impact study on human health and the ecosystem, and public participation in decisions about the territory.</p>","fontes":[["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/nao-conseguimos-respirar-movimento-alega-problemas-em-cercal-do-alentejo-devido-a-incendio-em-fabrica-de-pellets"],["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/incendio-na-fabrica-de-pellets-em-cercal-do-alentejo-continua-ativo_n1670870"],["Notícias ao Minuto","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/2834597/movimento-alega-problemas-respiratorios-em-cercal-do-alentejo"]],"stat":"230+ signatures","link":"https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/nao-conseguimos-respirar-movimento-alega-problemas-em-cercal-do-alentejo-devido-a-incendio-em-fabrica-de-pellets","linkL":"Read on Correio da Manhã"},"pedreira-lajedo-santo-tirso":{"corpo":"<p>The Lajedo quarry, in Monte Córdova, Santo Tirso, sat inactive for over ten years until it was reactivated in 2024, with an illegal expansion into an ecological reserve zone. For decades, residents complained of blasts that cracked walls and threw stones onto roofs, on top of noise and pressure on soils and water resources.</p>\n<p>A group of citizens launched a public petition demanding the permanent closure of the quarry, arguing that the operation undermines the well-being and quality of life of the local population. In March 2026, the company operating the quarry went as far as threatening to cut off a public road that had been in use for 30 years.</p>\n<p>The dispute between the company and residents remains unresolved, with Santo Tirso City Council also involved in the process.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal de Notícias","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/moradores-criaram-peticao-para-exigir-fim-de-pedreira-em-santo-tirso/17855057"],["Diário de Santo Tirso","https://www.diariodesantotirso.pt/peticao-publica-pelo-encerramento-da-pedreira-do-lajedo-ja-tem-de-350-assinaturas/"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/03/04/empresa-ameaca-cortar-estrada-publica-em-santo-tirso-para-operar-em-pedreira/"],["Jornal do Ave","https://jornaldoave.sapo.pt/cidadaos-lancam-peticao-contra-reativacao-da-pedreira-de-lajedo-em-monte-cordova/"]],"stat":"492+ signatures","link":"https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/moradores-criaram-peticao-para-exigir-fim-de-pedreira-em-santo-tirso/17855057","linkL":"Read on Jornal de Notícias"},"aranha-cavernicola-arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>Anapistula ataecina, known as the Frade cave spider, is Europe's smallest spider, measuring under half a millimetre. It lives only in the karst system of Frade, in Sesimbra, inside the Arrábida Natural Park; males of the species have never been observed, as reproduction is parthenogenetic.</p>\n<p>The International Union for Conservation of Nature classifies the species as Critically Endangered, the highest threat level. With such a restricted range, the presence of quarries within its distribution area, and the risk of their expansion, is identified as the main threat to the species' survival.</p>\n<p>The petition, addressed to Parliament and to ICNF, calls for concrete measures to protect the species' cave habitat, in a natural park where we already document other causes linked to quarrying activity.</p>","fontes":[["Naturdata","https://naturdata.com/aranha-endemica-de-portugal-classificada-pela-iucn-como-criticamente-em-perigo-de-extincao/"],["GreenSavers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/sabia-que-a-aranha-mais-pequena-da-europa-vive-em-portugal/"],["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/pelo-menos-mais-de-200-especies-de-invertebrados-em-risco-de-extincao-em-portugal/87085"]],"stat":"33+ signatures","link":"https://naturdata.com/aranha-endemica-de-portugal-classificada-pela-iucn-como-criticamente-em-perigo-de-extincao/","linkL":"Read on Naturdata"},"trilhos-madeira":{"corpo":"<p>The Regional Government of Madeira decided to hand over management of access to hiking trails to private entities, contracting the security company Strong Charon for 320,000 euros, from April to December, to control access to sites such as Pico do Areeiro, Ribeiro Frio, Achada do Teixeira, Queimadas and Ponta de São Lourenço.</p>\n<p>Citizens concerned with preserving the Autonomous Region's natural, cultural and social heritage are speaking out against any privatisation, concession or abusive restriction of public access to the trails. The LIVRE party also publicly spoke out against the measure, calling it \"an attack on public natural heritage\".</p>\n<p>Critics point above all to the lack of public consultation, transparency or democratic debate before the Regional Government's decision.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal da Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/livre-continua-a-opor-se-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres-e-apela-a-intervencao-da-sociedade-civil-DN18407422"],["Funchal Notícias","https://funchalnoticias.net/2025/06/24/livre-madeira-mantem-oposicao-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125916"]],"stat":"1,109+ signatures","link":"https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/livre-continua-a-opor-se-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres-e-apela-a-intervencao-da-sociedade-civil-DN18407422","linkL":"Read on Jornal da Madeira"},"mina-gudina":{"corpo":"<p>Just a few kilometres from the Portuguese border, in Pentes, in the municipality of A Gudiña, in the Galician province of Ourense, the company Tungsten San Juan, a subsidiary of Sweden's Eurobattery Minerals, is preparing an open-pit tungsten mine, with production expected in the fourth quarter of 2026 and reserves estimated at 60,000 tonnes. The mine sits about 100 metres from the Ribeira de Pente stream, which flows into the Rabaçal river in Vinhais, Bragança district, supplying water to fourteen Portuguese villages inside Montesinho Natural Park.</p>\n<p>Movimento UIVO, based in Vinhais, says the cross-border environmental impact assessment required under the Espoo Convention has never been carried out, even though the European Commission confirmed the obligation in July 2026. On 23 July, around 40 Portuguese and Galician environmentalists and local officials, including members of Ecoloxistas en Acción, gathered outside the church of San Martiño in A Gudiña to demand the assessment and delivered a letter to the Spanish municipality's mayor.</p>\n<p>Meanwhile, a court in Santiago de Compostela opened an investigation into the 30-year extension of the mining concession, following a complaint from Ecoloxistas en Acción. Parish officials in Vinhais say residents have stopped drinking tap water for fear of contamination, and the Portuguese government admits it has never been consulted by Spain about the project's impacts on national territory.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/ecologistas-e-autarcas-protestam-em-a-gudina-contra-mina-junto-a-fronteira-com-portugal"],["Mensageiro de Bragança","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/ambientalistas-portugueses-e-galegos-protestam-contra-mina-junto-fronteira-de-vinhais"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/19/uivo-acusa-espanha-de-violar-acordos-bilaterais-e-admite-recorrer-aos-tribunais-para-travar-exploracao-junto-a-fronteira-portuguesa/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/movimento-alerta-para-mina-espanhola-junto-a-vinhais-que-pode-ameacar-o-rio-rabacal-e-o-parque-natural-de-montesinho"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/07/bruxelas-confirma-obrigatoriedade-de-declaracao-ambiental-transfronteirica-para-mina-na-gudina/"]],"stat":"14 villages rely on the Rabaçal river","link":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/ecologistas-e-autarcas-protestam-em-a-gudina-contra-mina-junto-a-fronteira-com-portugal","linkL":"Read in Diário de Trás-os-Montes"},"alqueva-solar-flutuante":{"corpo":"<p>In 2022, EDP Renováveis won the largest lot in Portugal's national floating solar auction, securing the right to install 70 megawatts of photovoltaic capacity on the Alqueva reservoir, bidding a negative price of €4 per megawatt-hour. The project, named \"Grande Lago\", envisaged a hybrid plant of up to 154 MW, combining floating panels, additional solar capacity and a wind farm, across an area that would have covered 250 hectares of the reservoir's surface, spanning the municipalities of Moura, Portel and Reguengos de Monsaraz.</p>\n<p>In November 2025, the mayors of Moura, Reguengos de Monsaraz, Portel, Alandroal and Mourão met with the Minister of Environment and Energy to oppose the project, warning that a reservoir \"packed with solar panels\" would harm tourism and navigability in the region and bring \"no added value\" to the municipalities involved.</p>\n<p>On 6 August 2026, EDP announced it was dropping the project, citing profitability concerns after the Portuguese Environment Agency rejected the environmental impact study, notably over the impact of the grid connection line on birds of prey habitats. The case adds to a string of floating solar projects rejected on environmental grounds in Portuguese reservoirs since the 2022 auction.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/11/28/cinco-camaras-contestam-nova-central-fotovoltaica-flutuante-no-alqueva/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/edp-ganha-maior-lote-no-leilao-solar-flutuante-e-vai-instalar-mega-central-no-alqueva"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/06/grupo-edp-deixa-cair-central-solar-flutuante-no-alqueva-por-questoes-de-rentabilidade-e-apos-chumbo-de-estudo-ambiental/"],["Observador: especial solar flutuante","https://observador.pt/especiais/solar-flutuante-com-escala-ainda-e-uma-miragem-porque-estao-a-ser-chumbadas-as-centrais-em-cima-de-barragens/"]],"stat":"154 MW cancelled","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/11/28/cinco-camaras-contestam-nova-central-fotovoltaica-flutuante-no-alqueva/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"predios-madeira":{"corpo":"<p>Madeira's Regional Government president, Miguel Albuquerque, defended revising Funchal's Municipal Master Plan (PDM) to allow residential buildings up to 20 storeys, as a response to the shortage of available land for housing. Funchal City Council came out in support of the proposal.</p>\n<p>In response, more than 1,700 citizens signed the petition \"Pela Salvaguarda do Modelo Urbano da Madeira\" (\"For the Safeguard of Madeira's Urban Model\"), asking parties represented in the regional parliament to recommend that the Government not approve legislative, regulatory or territorial planning changes that would, as a general rule, allow buildings over ten storeys in the region. The petitioners instead call for urban rehabilitation policies, reuse of vacant buildings and regeneration of already built-up areas.</p>\n<p>According to the petition, defining Madeira's urban model \"is a generational decision, whose effects will last for decades,\" and should be preceded by a broad public debate involving universities, professional associations, local authorities and experts in urban planning, architecture and the environment. Miguel Albuquerque downplayed the opposition, saying the proposal would only allow high-rise construction \"in areas with no landscape impact.\"</p>","fontes":[["Espaço de Arquitetura","https://espacodearquitetura.com/noticias/peticao-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira/"],["DNOTICIAS","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2026/7/24/500243-peticao-contra-construcao-em-altura-a-caminho-da-assembleia/"],["Observador: Albuquerque defende revisão do PDM","https://observador.pt/2026/07/15/albuquerque-defende-revisao-do-pdm-para-permitir-predios-de-habitacao-em-altura-no-funchal/"],["Observador: Câmara do Funchal apoia","https://observador.pt/2026/07/16/camara-do-funchal-apoia-construcao-de-predios-de-habitacao-em-altura-no-concelho/"],["JM Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/not%C3%ADcias/regi-o/30002568/mais-de-1-700-peticionarios-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira.html"],["SAPO Notícias","https://sapo.pt/artigo/peticao-contra-edificios-em-altura-na-madeira-atinge-mil-assinaturas-6a5cb85ec3fc30cdb0f69f0b"]],"stat":"1,700+ signatures","link":"https://espacodearquitetura.com/noticias/peticao-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira/","linkL":"Read on Espaço de Arquitetura"},"eolico-sudoeste-sines":{"corpo":"<p>Hyperion Renewables Sines wants to build the Southwest Wind Farm, split into three clusters, São Bartolomeu, Vale Miguel and Monte das Oliveiras, between Santiago do Cacém and Cercal do Alentejo. The project envisages 23 to 31 turbines over 100 metres tall, 138 MW of total capacity, an estimated annual output of 386.4 GWh, and a storage system of 61 lithium battery containers with 200 MWh of capacity, across a 1,098.4-hectare study area. The energy is intended almost exclusively to power the Start Campus Data Center in Sines, which at full capacity could consume up to 20% of the electricity used in Portugal.</p>\n<p>Quercus warns that the document under public consultation systematically classifies impacts as \"of little significance\" despite affecting classified habitats, such as cork and holm oak groves, dry European heathlands and watercourses, legally protected cork and holm oaks, bird and bat mortality from collisions, and disturbance to nationally protected agricultural and ecological reserve areas. The association also found, on page 96 of the document, a reference to energy production \"from the sun\": a sign, it says, that the study was hastily copy-pasted from another process, symptomatic of assembly-line environmental impact studies with little rigour.</p>\n<p>The citizen movement RENOVAR Santiago do Cacém also opposes the project, criticising that the public consultation is running during the summer holiday period with little involvement from affected communities. The movement notes the municipality already hosts two other large contested solar projects: about 1,260 hectares between São Domingos and Vale de Água, and about 394 hectares in Cercal do Alentejo. It is calling for a cumulative impact study covering all the energy megaprojects planned for the region. The public consultation on the proposed scope of the environmental impact study was open on the Participa portal until 18 August 2026.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/08/megaprojeto-eolico-em-santiago-do-cacem-ao-servico-da-ia-quercus-alerta-para-impactos-ambientais-subavaliados/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/08/quercus-alerta-para-subavaliacao-de-impacto-de-parque-eolico-para-alimentar-centro-de-dados-de-sines/"],["Executive Digest","https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/parque-eolico-com-23-aerogeradores-em-santiago-do-cacem-em-consulta-publica/"],["Rádio Campanário: RENOVAR Santiago do Cacém","https://www.radiocampanario.com/renovar-santiago-do-cacem-critica-projeto-do-parque-eolico-do-sudoeste-e-exige-maior-envolvimento-das-populacoes/"],["Rádio Campanário: underassessed impacts","https://www.radiocampanario.com/associacao-ambientalista-alerta-para-subavaliacao-de-impactos-ambientais-de-parque-eolico/"]],"stat":"1,098 hectares · up to 31 turbines","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/08/megaprojeto-eolico-em-santiago-do-cacem-ao-servico-da-ia-quercus-alerta-para-impactos-ambientais-subavaliados/","linkL":""},"vigilantes-natureza":{"corpo":"<p>The Portuguese Confederation of Environmental Defence Associations (CPADA) recommended that the Government urgently hire new Nature Wardens and review their career track, which has not been updated in more than 20 years. According to 2024 data, the Institute for Nature Conservation and Forests (ICNF) had just 286 nature wardens, when the reference defended by the professional association of the class is 800: 600 on the mainland and 200 in the autonomous regions. The current 286 represent about 11% of ICNF's total staff and correspond to more than 2,500 hectares to protect per warden.</p>\n<p>CPADA warns that this shortage of staff limits response capacity, undermines compliance with conservation targets, and hampers proper monitoring and rapid intervention against threats such as forest fires and deforestation. The confederation also calls for better pay conditions, clear career progression, and proper uniforms and personal protective equipment.</p>\n<p>The request comes as the Government negotiates an agreement, dated June 2026, that would merge the forest ranger and nature warden careers into a new Forest and Environmental Guard category. Ninety wardens signed a letter to the Environment Minister asking for the agreement to be revised, citing pay inequalities, disparities in risk allowances and retirement age, and the devaluation of professional experience. The National Union of Civil Protection also refused to sign the agreement and says it may ask the Government to halt it.</p>","fontes":[["Green Savers (Lusa)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/associacoes-de-ambiente-pedem-contratacao-urgente-de-vigilantes-da-natureza/"],["Notícias ao Minuto","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3031535/associacoes-de-ambiente-pedem-contratacao-urgente-de-vigilantes"],["Ambiente Magazine","https://www.ambientemagazine.com/cpada-pede-reforco-para-800-vigilantes-da-natureza-e-revisao-urgente-da-carreira/"],["Diário de Viseu (Lusa)","https://www.diarioviseu.pt/2026/08/04/vigilantes-da-natureza-contra-extincao-de-carreira/"]],"stat":"286 wardens · should be 800","link":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/associacoes-de-ambiente-pedem-contratacao-urgente-de-vigilantes-da-natureza/","linkL":"Read on greensavers.sapo.pt"},"hyperion-abrantes":{"corpo":"<p>Hyperion II Renewables Services wants to build the second large-scale data center next to the Pego power plant, in Abrantes, already holding National Interest Project (PIN) status. The project envisages a 200 MVA connection capacity on over 1 million square metres of land, of which 15 hectares are earmarked for construction, with a planned start in 2029.</p>\n<p>Abrantes Municipal Council unanimously approved the project's preliminary request in May 2026. The Portuguese Environment Agency made its approval conditional on the submission of a complete environmental impact study, but only at the next licensing stage: in other words, the process moved forward before a full environmental assessment of the project existed.</p>\n<p>PIN status speeds up licensing and gives the developer a single point of contact within the State. It is the same regime used for other data centers, mines and energy projects in Portugal, some already documented by Causas de Raiz.</p>","fontes":[["Correio do Ribatejo","https://correiodoribatejo.pt/abrantes-aprova-pedido-previo-para-segundo-centro-de-dados-junto-a-central-do-pego/"],["ECO: how the Government plans to attract more data centers","https://eco.sapo.pt/descodificador/como-o-governo-planeia-atrair-mais-data-centers-para-portugal/"]],"stat":"200 MVA connection capacity","link":"https://correiodoribatejo.pt/abrantes-aprova-pedido-previo-para-segundo-centro-de-dados-junto-a-central-do-pego/","linkL":"Read on Correio do Ribatejo"},"azambuja-dc":{"corpo":"<p>French company Neoen requested National Interest Project (PIN) status from AICEP for a data center valued at €2 billion, to be built in Alcoentre, a parish within Azambuja municipality.</p>\n<p>In July 2026, Azambuja Municipal Council gave an unfavourable opinion on the request, citing missing environmental, noise and landscape impact studies. The council's opinion is not binding: the final decision on PIN status is made at the national level, by AICEP, and the process remains open.</p>\n<p>The case illustrates a structural tension in the PIN regime: it speeds up licensing from Lisbon, even when the municipality where the project would be built objects for lack of environmental information.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/31/camara-de-azambuja-trava-estatuto-pin-para-data-center-de-2-mil-milhoes-de-euros/"]],"stat":"€2 billion investment","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/31/camara-de-azambuja-trava-estatuto-pin-para-data-center-de-2-mil-milhoes-de-euros/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"pego-transicao-justa":{"corpo":"<p>Endesa is moving forward with a €700 million project combining solar power, wind power and storage on the site of the former Pego coal-fired power plant, presented as part of the region's \"just transition\". The project already holds National Interest Project (PIN) status.</p>\n<p>Gavião Municipal Council unanimously rejected the project's PIN status. The council says the municipality already has about 2% of its territory covered by renewable energy projects and argues it is becoming a \"sacrifice zone\" serving the energy transition of other regions.</p>\n<p>The case adds to other energy and digital projects concentrated in the same area, next to the Pego power plant, including a second large-scale data center already reported (see the Hyperion II case, also documented by Causas de Raiz).</p>","fontes":[["Jornal de Abrantes","https://jornaldeabrantes.sapo.pt/economia/gaviao-contra-estatuto-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-de-transicao-justa-da-central-do-pego"]],"stat":"€700 million investment","link":"https://jornaldeabrantes.sapo.pt/economia/gaviao-contra-estatuto-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-de-transicao-justa-da-central-do-pego","linkL":"Read on Jornal de Abrantes"},"hidrogenio-sines":{"corpo":"<p>Sines concentrates several National Interest Project (PIN) status projects tied to hydrogen, ammonia and synthetic fuels: Madoqua H2, GreenH2Atlantic, Green Amonia Express, Navigator Green Fuels and MDQ Synfuels. They are part of the 13 projects in the \"chemical and petrochemical\" sector that, according to a 2024 business-press survey, represent the largest share of PIN projects granted in Portugal, alongside tourism.</p>\n<p>There is no public, official and complete list of all PIN projects in Portugal: sector figures come from AICEP statements to the press, not from an open registry. This cluster adds to two other cases already documented by Causas de Raiz in the same area, the AI gigafactory in Sines and the Southwest Wind Farm, both linked to the same pressure on water, energy and land on the Alentejo coast.</p>\n<p>As of this research, we did not identify a citizen organisation specifically monitoring this hydrogen cluster. It is recorded here as an alert, for ongoing monitoring.</p>","fontes":[["ECO: 55 National Interest Projects","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/08/13/portugal-acompanha-55-projetos-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-maioria-e-de-capital-estrangeiro/"],["ECO: how the Government plans to attract more data centers","https://eco.sapo.pt/descodificador/como-o-governo-planeia-atrair-mais-data-centers-para-portugal/"]],"stat":"5 PIN projects in Sines","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/08/13/portugal-acompanha-55-projetos-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-maioria-e-de-capital-estrangeiro/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"central-eolica-fronteira":{"corpo":"<p>The Fronteira Wind Farm plans to install 35 wind turbines, with 157.5 MW of installed capacity, in a 5,893-hectare study area across the municipalities of Vimioso and Miranda do Douro. The project is designed as a hybrid with the Picote Hydroelectric Plant, sharing its grid connection point.</p>\n<p>The study area overlaps the Douro Internacional Natural Park and three Natura 2000 Special Conservation Areas. The proposal that was in consultation defined the scope of the future environmental impact study, in other words, what will (or will not) be assessed in depth before licensing.</p>\n<p>Miranda do Douro Municipal Council made the consultation public; it ran on the Participa portal until August 17, 2026. The final scope of the environmental impact study follows next.</p>","fontes":[["Miranda do Douro Municipal Council","https://www.cm-mdouro.pt/municipio/comunicacao/noticias/noticia/consulta-publica-projeto-da-central-eolica-da-fronteira"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/28/central-eolica-da-fronteira-em-vimioso-com-5-893-hectares-em-area-de-estudo/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/central-eolica-da-fronteira-em-vimioso-com-5893-hectares-de-area-de-estudo"]],"stat":"5,893 hectares in the study area","link":"https://www.cm-mdouro.pt/municipio/comunicacao/noticias/noticia/consulta-publica-projeto-da-central-eolica-da-fronteira","linkL":"Read on the Miranda do Douro Council website"},"descontaminacao-ilha-terceira":{"corpo":"<p>Over nearly seven decades, the US military presence at Lajes Base, on Terceira Island, left dozens of contaminated sites, documented by the Portuguese Air Force and the National Civil Engineering Laboratory (LNEC). Between 2020 and 2022, the United States carried out no remediation work, holding that the soil and aquifer contamination was not harmful to health.</p>\n<p>The decontamination process is stuck in a diplomatic deadlock, with neither Portugal nor the United States taking on concrete responsibility. An active public petition calls for effective environmental decontamination of the island's soils and aquifers.</p>\n<p>The Azores Parliament approved, with support from several parties, the creation of an Independent Technical Committee to oversee, monitor and evaluate the process. The Azores branch of the Socialist Party and the Left Bloc have asked the national Government for updated information and political priority on the issue.</p>","fontes":[["Green Savers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/pela-descontaminacao-ambiental-dos-solos-e-aquiferos-da-ilha-terceira-ha-peticao-publica-online/"],["Observador: independent committee","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/acores-criam-comissao-independente-para-fiscalizar-descontaminacao-dos-solos-na-ilha-terceira-junto-a-base-das-lajes/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/portugal/detalhe/acores-solicitam-documentacao-sobre-descontaminacao-de-solos-e-aquiferos-ao-governo-da-republica"]],"stat":"Nearly 7 decades of contamination","link":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/pela-descontaminacao-ambiental-dos-solos-e-aquiferos-da-ilha-terceira-ha-peticao-publica-online/","linkL":"Read on greensavers.sapo.pt"},"linha-atalaia-cruzeiro-concavada":{"corpo":"<p>The Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA no. 3736) of the Atalaia-Torre das Vargens power line and the Cruzeiro-Concavada line branch, promoted by Endesa Generación Portugal, was in public consultation until August 18, 2026. These lines are part of the so-called Pego Cluster, the set of four groups of solar, wind and storage projects with which Endesa occupies the former Pego coal-fired power plant site, across the municipalities of Abrantes, Gavião and Ponte de Sor.</p>\n<p>CHIRO, a Portuguese bat conservation association, objected to a reformulation of the related Atalaia-Concavada solar project, asking for monitoring of bat populations before, during and after construction, and for the preservation of the main feeding areas and shelters identified.</p>\n<p>The case adds to two others already documented by Causas de Raiz in the same area, next to the Pego power plant: the Hyperion II data center and the \"Just Transition\" project contested by Gavião Council.</p>","fontes":[["Gavião Municipal Council","https://cm-gaviao.pt/apa-consulta-publica-projeto-solar-de-atalaia-concavada-e-linhas-eletricas-de-interligacao-220kv-via-se-comenda-e-cruzeiro/"],["Public Consultation Report, EIA no. 3736 (APA)","https://siaia.apambiente.pt/AIADOC/AIA3736/rel_cp202615102631.pdf"]],"stat":"EIA no. 3736","link":"https://cm-gaviao.pt/apa-consulta-publica-projeto-solar-de-atalaia-concavada-e-linhas-eletricas-de-interligacao-220kv-via-se-comenda-e-cruzeiro/","linkL":"Read on the Gavião Council website"},"jardins-se-porto":{"corpo":"<p>A public petition, \"Not even the Cathedral is safe?\", has gathered over 1,800 signatures calling for the preservation of the Diocese gardens on Porto's Sé hill. According to the petitioners, the Major Seminary gardens will disappear under a new construction started by the Cathedral and the Seminary, whose owners changed a project approved as \"monastic accommodation\" into a 3-star hotel, keeping essentially the same building.</p>\n<p>Porto City Council intends to refuse the local accommodation licence for the development, holding that the Seminary's current function is not compatible with a fully independent and autonomous hotel activity.</p>\n<p>The Diocese of Porto says it is in dialogue with the council to find solutions that fit within the building permit already issued by the Council and that respect the site, located in Porto's historic centre.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/peticao-com-mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pede-preservacao-dos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/"],["Viva Porto","https://viva-porto.pt/mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pedem-para-travar-hotel-nos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/"]],"stat":"1,800+ signatures","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/peticao-com-mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pede-preservacao-dos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"rio-almansor":{"corpo":"<p>The Almansor River rises near Arraiolos and runs 97 kilometres before flowing into the Sorraia, passing through Montemor-o-Novo, Vendas Novas, Canha and Santo Estêvão. For decades it has received pollutant loads well above the regional average, from urban sewage, intensive agriculture and pig farming, leading Portugal's water authority to rate its quality as \"Below Good\", with no significant change for years.</p>\n<p>In 2024, after a sewage system failure in Montemor-o-Novo, residents along the riverbank organized and founded AMORA, an association run through horizontal, deliberative democracy. That same year, the first ever Water Management Plan for the Almansor was approved in Portugal, and the municipality created its first ever municipal environmental council. AGDA, the sanitation utility, was fined €130,000 for negligence, a decision it has appealed.</p>\n<p>Water tests carried out by residents along the river found high levels of fecal coliforms, excess nutrients and microplastics. AMORA maps pollution sources, takes part in public consultations and mobilizes the community to clean and regenerate the river, aiming to make it swimmable again within five years.</p>","fontes":[["AMORA - The Almansor","https://amoralmansor.pt/o-almansor/"],["Montemor-o-Novo Municipal Council","https://www.cm-montemornovo.pt/comunicado-valorizacao-do-rio-almansor-e-garantia-da-qualidade-da-agua-no-concelho/"],["Spring Prize","https://springprize.org/shortlisted/associacao-de-moradores-do-rio-almansor-amora/"]],"stat":"€130,000 fine against AGDA (under appeal)","link":"https://amoralmansor.pt","linkL":"Learn more at amoralmansor.pt"},"fernando-pessoa":{"corpo":"<p>The Fernando Pessoa Photovoltaic Plant, developed by Iberdrola in partnership with Prosolia, was approved by the Portuguese Environment Agency in January 2023 as Europe's largest solar plant and the fifth largest in the world: 1,200 megawatts of installed capacity across roughly a thousand hectares in the municipality of Santiago do Cacém, near Sines. Construction involves felling around 1.5 million trees, mostly eucalyptus.</p>\n<p>The ProtegeAlentejo association argues the Environmental Impact Statement was approved despite unfavourable opinions from the Institute for Nature Conservation and Forests, the National Laboratory of Energy and Geology, and even the agency's own head of environmental impact assessment. In January 2024, the Public Prosecutor's Office filed a case at the Administrative and Fiscal Court of Beja against the agency's licence, arguing it disregarded a wide range of land-use and natural resource protection rules.</p>\n<p>More than two years on, the case still awaits a first-instance ruling, even though the agency has appealed. Construction, which Iberdrola once expected to finish by 2025, remains suspended by the courts.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/24/maior-central-solar-da-europa-travada-pela-justica/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/03/25/sociedade/noticia/associacao-protegealentejo-satisfeita-accao-mp-central-solar-santiago-cacem-2084850"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/solar-park-projects-pushed-through-without-transparency/"]],"stat":"1,200 MW · Europe's largest solar plant","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"dessalinizadora-albufeira":{"corpo":"<p>The Algarve Seawater Desalination Plant, under construction next to Praia da Rocha Baixinha in Albufeira, represents an investment of over €100 million, financed through the Recovery and Resilience Plan. The Águas do Algarve project aims to convert an initial 16 million cubic metres of seawater into drinking water per year, potentially rising to 24 million.</p>\n<p>The project has already faced two court injunctions. In 2025, associations linked to the Sustainable Water Platform, including Almargem and A Rocha Portugal, unsuccessfully challenged the length of the public consultation on the Execution Project's Environmental Compliance Report. In April 2026, with construction already under way, Seacliff, the former owner of the expropriated land where the plant is being built, filed a new injunction at the Administrative and Fiscal Court of Loulé, with immediate suspensive effect on construction.</p>\n<p>Fishermen from Albufeira and Quarteira, together with Albufeira's mayor, joined a protest at Praia da Rocha Baixinha, calling for a fuller assessment of the impacts on the sea and local fishing. Despite the opposition, the Environment Minister insists the project will proceed, and Águas do Algarve expects to complete the plant within about two years.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/04/dessalinizadora-no-algarve-alvo-de-mais-uma-providencia-cautelar/"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/dessalinizadora-do-algarve-esta-a-avancar-e-devera-estar-concluida-em-dois-anos/"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2026-05-04/construction-of-desalination-plant-in-the-algarve-has-been-suspended/1016802"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/algarve/seacliff-denuncia-continuacao-de-obras-na-dessalinizadora-mas-aguas-do-algarve-nega/"]],"stat":"€100+ million","link":"https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/dessalinizadora-do-algarve-esta-a-avancar-e-devera-estar-concluida-em-dois-anos/","linkL":"Read on Sul Informação"},"mina-panasqueira":{"corpo":"<p>The Panasqueira Mines, operating for over a century across the municipalities of Covilhã and Fundão, are among Europe's oldest and most productive tin and tungsten mines, currently run by Beralt Tin and Wolfram Portugal. In January 2026, heavy rain caused another collapse in the mine's tailings structure, sweeping toxic inert waste into the Cebola stream, a tributary of the Zêzere River.</p>\n<p>Quercus warned of highly toxic heavy metals, including lead and arsenic, also detected along the banks of the Zêzere itself. The incident led to the suspension of water intake at a local supply point and forced Covilhã's municipal council to step up water quality testing.</p>\n<p>The association notes that the Castelo do Bode Dam, on the Zêzere, supplies water to the Greater Lisbon area, and is calling on the Portuguese Environment Agency, the water regulator ERSAR and the Inspectorate-General of Agriculture, Sea, Environment and Land Use Planning for stronger oversight, while demanding that Beralt remediate the tailings, expand wastewater treatment capacity and carry out regular maintenance of the pipes carrying toxic effluent.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/03/24/alerta-para-risco-de-contaminacao-do-rio-zezere/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/03/24/azul/noticia/minas-panasqueira-quercus-denuncia-risco-contaminacao-toxica-rio-zezere-2163617"],["JN","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/quercus-pede-fiscalizacao-a-agua-do-zezere-por-receio-de-contaminacao-com-residuos-da-panasqueira/18065748"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/concerns-for-lisbon-drinking-water-following-repeated-mining-waste-collapse/"]],"stat":"Lead and arsenic in the Zêzere","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/03/24/alerta-para-risco-de-contaminacao-do-rio-zezere/","linkL":"Read Quercus' statement"},"mina-borralha":{"corpo":"<p>The association Povo e Natureza do Barroso has filed a legal action against the Environmental Impact Statement for the Borralha mine project in Montalegre, Vila Real district. The action also represents the Movimento Não às Minas – Montalegre, the governing councils of the Caniçó, Linharelhos and Campos commons, Iris (National Environment Association) and APIFC. The project, to mine tungsten through underground galleries inactive since 1986, received a conditional favourable opinion from the Portuguese Environment Agency in January 2026, with the concession held by the company Minerália; Montalegre's municipal council had already issued a negative opinion.</p>\n<p>The area lies within the Gerês-Xurés Transboundary Biosphere Reserve, six kilometres from Peneda-Gerês National Park, and is part of the FAO's Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System, in one of northern Portugal's most important water resource areas. The associations warn of the risk to the Rabagão water treatment plant, located downstream of the project, and of the unresolved environmental liability from the old Borralha mine, still pending four decades after its closure.</p>\n<p>The public consultation on the environmental impact study, held between October and November 2025, received 653 submissions, many concerning drinking water intake at the Venda Nova dam downstream of the mine. The associations also report unanswered complaints about pollution in the Amiar stream. Minerália says it will use 100% recycled water, with no abstraction from rivers, dams or aquifers.</p>","fontes":[["O Minho / Lusa","https://ominho.pt/associacao-interpoe-acao-judicial-contra-avaliacao-ambiental-da-mina-em-montalegre/"],["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/camara-de-montalegre-da-parecer-negativo-a-exploracao-mineira-na-borralha_n1698959"],["SÁBADO","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/20251118-101859-camara-de-montalegre-da-parecer-negativo-a-exploracao-mineira-na-borralha"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/apa-aprova-projeto-da-mina-da-borralha-com-condicoes-ambientais"]],"stat":"653 public consultation submissions","link":"https://ominho.pt/associacao-interpoe-acao-judicial-contra-avaliacao-ambiental-da-mina-em-montalegre/","linkL":"Read on O Minho"},"almaraz":{"corpo":"<p>Spain's Ministry for Ecological Transition renewed the operating licence for Units I and II of the Almaraz Nuclear Power Plant, in Cáceres, in the Tagus river basin, about 100 kilometres from the Portuguese border, until June 2030. The decision follows a formal request for the extension made in October 2025 by the plant's three owners, Iberdrola, Endesa and Naturgy.</p>\n<p>The gradual shutdown of the two reactors, operating since the early 1980s, had been scheduled for November 2027 (Unit I) and October 2028 (Unit II), under a protocol already agreed between the companies and the Spanish state. The movement \"Alargar as Nucleares, Não Obrigado\" (\"Extend Nuclear Plants, No Thanks\"), which brings together Adenex, Ecologistas en Acción and Greenpeace, calls the extension \"illegal\" for breaking that agreement.</p>\n<p>The Iberian Energy Observatory, which brings together Portuguese and Spanish associations, announced it will go to court \"as soon as possible\" against the decision, with the case to be filed in Spain by Adenex. The associations warn that extending Almaraz could also jeopardise the shutdown schedule for Spain's other nuclear plants.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/nacional/2026-08-14-associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz-3acf4579"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/14/associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-nuclear-de-almaraz/"],["DN","https://www.dn.pt/internacional/associaes-avanam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz"],["Infobae (Spain)","https://www.infobae.com/espana/agencias/2026/08/16/ecologistas-extremadura-recurre-la-orden-de-prorroga-de-la-central-nuclear-de-almaraz/"]],"stat":"Licence extended to 2030","link":"https://omirante.pt/nacional/2026-08-14-associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz-3acf4579","linkL":"Read on O Mirante"},"citrinos-alcacer-do-sal":{"corpo":"<p>The Aquaterra group, linked to a North American investment fund, received a conditional Environmental Impact Statement on 3 August 2026 for an intensive tangerine farming project across roughly 295 hectares at the Murta and Monte Novo estates, in Alcácer do Sal. It is the fourth version of the project: the previous three, which proposed 722 hectares of avocado, were all rejected.</p>\n<p>The site lies within the Natura 2000 network, in the Comporta/Galé Special Conservation Area, over an aquifer already in critical condition, with land subsidence and rising piezometric pressure. The project still depends on groundwater abstraction through 12 deep boreholes. Alentejo's regional environmental authority approved the statement despite an unfavourable opinion from Quercus and despite 99.2% of public consultation submissions rejecting the project; ZERO called the decision a \"gross error\".</p>\n<p>Quercus will file a formal complaint with the European Commission for breach of EU law, calling for the protection of the Comporta-Galé conservation area and the region's aquifers, and is considering an injunction at Portugal's administrative courts to suspend the statement. The association is also demanding an independent opinion from the National Laboratory of Energy and Geology on the aquifer and the resumption of the National Water Council, which hasn't met in three years.</p>","fontes":[["Wilder","https://wilder.pt/historias/quercus-apresenta-queixa-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-de-citrinos-em-alcacer-do-sal"],["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/14/projeto-citrinos-alcacer-do-sal/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/13/luz-verde-dada-a-projeto-de-tangerinas-que-substitui-abacates-em-alcacer-do-sal-e-erro-grosseiro-diz-a-zero/"],["GreenSavers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/zero-considera-erro-grosseiro-luz-verde-a-projeto-de-tangerinas-em-alcacer-do-sal/"]],"stat":"99.2% of public consultation against the project","link":"https://wilder.pt/historias/quercus-apresenta-queixa-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-de-citrinos-em-alcacer-do-sal","linkL":"Read on Wilder"},"rio-corgo-vila-real":{"corpo":"<p>The Portuguese Environment Agency (APA) is investigating the death of dozens of fish recorded in the Corgo River, in Vila Real municipality, in an action carried out together with the GNR's Nature and Environment Protection Service (SEPNA). Water samples and dead fish specimens were collected for laboratory analysis.</p>\n<p>The authorities' preliminary assessment points to a probable abnormal wastewater discharge, whose source is still being determined, that entered the watercourse through the stormwater drainage network. The pollution event appears to have been a one-off, between 15 and 16 August 2026, days with thunderstorms and rain in the region; combined with high temperatures and the low summer flow typical of the season, this likely triggered the fish kill.</p>\n<p>APA continues to monitor the situation on the ground and is awaiting laboratory reports to determine the exact extent of the ecological damage and the source of the discharge.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/apa-investiga-causas-da-morte-de-peixes-no-rio-corgo-em-vila-real"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/19/descarga-de-aguas-residuais-podera-ter-causado-morte-de-peixes-em-rio-de-vila-real/"]],"stat":"One-off discharge on 15-16 August 2026","link":"https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/apa-investiga-causas-da-morte-de-peixes-no-rio-corgo-em-vila-real","linkL":"Read on Diário de Notícias"},"rio-eiriz-meixomil":{"corpo":"<p>A polluting discharge recorded in the early hours of a Sunday in August 2026 in the Eiriz River, next to Meixomil's Urban Park, killed dozens of fish. The Meixomil Parish Council announced it would file a complaint with the competent authorities to determine the source of the contamination.</p>\n<p>The subsequent investigation identified the cause: a malfunction in a clogged sewage collector on Rua da Agra, in the parish of Eiriz, which caused effluent to accidentally overflow into the watercourse. The possibility of intentional or deliberate pollution was ruled out.</p>\n<p>The utility Águas de Paços de Ferreira unblocked the collector and is carrying out a river clean-up operation, including removal of sludge and waste from the discharge.</p>","fontes":[["Imediato (discharge)","https://www.imediato.pt/descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-provoca-morte-de-dezenas-de-peixes-em-meixomil/"],["Imediato (cause)","https://www.imediato.pt/avaria-em-coletor-de-saneamento-na-origem-da-mortalidade-de-peixes-no-rio-eiriz/"],["Novum Canal","https://novumcanal.pt/2026/08/avaria-em-coletor-esteve-na-origem-da-descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-que-provocou-a-morte-a-dezenas-de-peixes/"]],"stat":"Dozens of dead fish · malfunction confirmed, no sign of intentional discharge","link":"https://www.imediato.pt/descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-provoca-morte-de-dezenas-de-peixes-em-meixomil/","linkL":"Read on Imediato"},"pedreiras-beja":{"corpo":"<p>Bairro das Pedreiras was opened in January 2006 by Beja City Council to rehouse about 50 families, roughly two hundred people, who had been living in shacks in the Bairro da Esperança. What was meant to be a temporary solution became permanent: two decades on, dozens of self-built shacks have sprung up around the original brick houses, without piped water, sanitation or electricity.</p>\n<p>According to Público, about a thousand people, over 200 children among them, live in conditions the newspaper describes as \"sub-human\": no drinking water, accumulated rubbish, dry scrub where snakes and rats breed, and temperatures above 38°C in summer with no relief. The neighbourhood sits next to the council's kennel and materials yard: the animal shelter's facilities were renovated while the families remain in shacks.</p>\n<p>Beja City Council carried out a new survey of the neighbourhood in 2025, but residents and journalists point to two decades of neglect by successive local and national governments. The Portuguese press describes the case as anticiganismo (anti-Roma discrimination). Internationally, the same pattern, basic environmental infrastructure denied to a racialized community, is called environmental racism: a term still rarely used in Portugal, but one that describes exactly the same phenomenon.</p>","fontes":[["Público (2023)","https://www.publico.pt/2023/08/22/local/noticia/familias-ciganas-beja-vivem-barracas-animais-dispoem-novas-instalacoes-2060768"],["Público (2018)","https://www.publico.pt/2018/01/23/local/noticia/secretarias-de-estado-chocadas-com-condicoes-da-comunidade-cigana-no-bairro-das-pedreiras-1800469"],["Diário do Alentejo","https://diariodoalentejo.pt/pt/noticias/22183/camara-de-beja-faz-novo-levantamento-do-bairro-das-pedreiras.aspx"],["Jornal Mapa","https://www.jornalmapa.pt/2025/12/08/habitar-na-precariedade-o-anticiganismo-que-se-constroi-em-betao-e-zinco/"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/fotoreportagem/pais/2025/10/08/os-invisiveis-ciganos-vivem-esquecidos-no-meio-do-lixo-em-beja/442175/"]],"stat":"About 1,000 people, over 200 children, without water or sanitation","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2023/08/22/local/noticia/familias-ciganas-beja-vivem-barracas-animais-dispoem-novas-instalacoes-2060768","linkL":"Read on Público"},"talude-militar-loures":{"corpo":"<p>Talude Militar was born in the 1980s, when Cape Verdean and São Tomean families working in construction around Lisbon began self-building homes on land in Loures, with no access to formal housing. More than 40 years on, the neighbourhood was never integrated or resolved by successive municipal governments.</p>\n<p>On July 14, 2025, Loures City Council launched a large-scale demolition operation targeting 64 structures where 161 people lived. 55 homes were demolished in two days; displaced families spent the night in tents and a church. On the third day, a court injunction filed by 14 residents led the Lisbon Administrative Court to suspend the operation.</p>\n<p>A year later, in July 2026, the deadlock remains: the council has demolished 88 homes since the operation began, but 23 are still protected by collective injunctions, and the Public Prosecutor's Office has opened an inquiry into the demolitions. None of the proceedings has reached a final outcome. Loures City Council has contested the court suspension.</p>\n<p>In the same municipality, the Santa Iria da Azóia neighbourhood, also mostly São Tomean, faced a 48-hour demolition notice in December 2024, later suspended at Social Security's request. The Portuguese press treats these cases as a housing crisis. But the pattern, decades of basic infrastructure denied and eviction without a housing alternative for racialized communities of African origin, is also environmental racism: a term rarely used in Portugal to describe a well-documented reality.</p>","fontes":[["Público (40-year-old neighbourhood)","https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/23/local/noticia/talude-militar-bairro-loures-nasceu-clandestino-ha-40-anos-resolveu-2141394"],["Observador (deadlock, Jul. 2026)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/14/vida-justa-faz-acusacoes-ao-presidente-da-camara-impasse-judicial-mantem-dezenas-de-barracas-em-pe-no-talude-militar-em-loures/"],["RTP (families in tents)","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/bairro-do-talude-familias-desalojadas-passam-noite-em-tendas-e-igreja_n1669173"],["Renascença (court suspends)","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2025/07/15/tribunal-impede-camara-de-loures-de-demolir-habitacoes-no-bairro-do-talude/432785/"],["Lisboa Para Pessoas (Santa Iria da Azóia)","https://lisboaparapessoas.pt/2024/12/16/despejo-em-loures-cerca-de-100-pessoas-sem-alternativa-habitacional/"],["AbrilAbril (Santa Iria da Azóia, follow-up)","https://www.abrilabril.pt/local/despejo-em-loures-continua-suspenso-mas-moradores-temem-janeiro"]],"stat":"88 homes demolished since July 2025 · 23 under court injunction · a year of legal deadlock","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/23/local/noticia/talude-militar-bairro-loures-nasceu-clandestino-ha-40-anos-resolveu-2141394","linkL":"Read on Público"},"penajoia-almada":{"corpo":"<p>The Penajóia neighbourhood, in Monte da Caparica, grew mainly over the past two years, on land belonging to IHRU, the Institute for Housing and Urban Rehabilitation. The housing crisis and unaffordable rents pushed families from Cape Verde, Angola and Guinea-Bissau, along with Brazilian and Portuguese families, into self-construction. About 160 households, roughly 350 people, now live in the neighbourhood, including 60 children, six newborns, 17 teenagers, elderly people, chronically ill residents and pregnant women, without public electricity, piped water or sanitation.</p>\n<p>IHRU began demolishing unfinished structures in January 2025. In December of that year, organizations again reported a case of forced demolition and eviction without rehousing: a family with three minor children was left without adequate housing after a demolition, and was even threatened with having the children removed while staying temporarily in a guesthouse.</p>\n<p>In December 2025, Almada City Council announced that the Ministry of Infrastructure and Housing would schedule a meeting for January to present a plan to halt the neighbourhood's expansion and find a housing solution. IHRU insists there will be no demolitions without alternative housing solutions, but residents, who wrote a letter to the council titled \"We are Almada too\", remain under threat.</p>\n<p>The same pattern documented in Beja and Loures repeats here: a racialized community, mostly of African origin, without access to basic environmental infrastructure, water, electricity, sanitation, and subject to evictions without a guaranteed housing alternative. This is environmental racism, even though the Portuguese press mostly frames it as a housing crisis.</p>","fontes":[["Renascença","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2024/12/10/bairro-da-penajoia-almada-se-tivesse-outras-condicoes-nao-estava-aqui/404757/"],["Observador (demolitions begin)","https://observador.pt/2025/01/23/irhu-comecou-esta-quinta-feira-a-demolir-construcoes-inacabadas-no-bairro-penajoia-em-almada/"],["Observador (forced eviction, Dec. 2025)","https://observador.pt/2025/12/20/organizacoes-denunciam-novo-caso-de-demolicao-e-despejo-forcado-sem-realojamento-em-almada/"],["Balai (Cape Verdean community)","https://www.balai.cv/noticias/sociedade/portugal-imigrantes-cabo-verdianos-dos-bairros-da-penajoia-e-raposo-em-almada-vivem-sob-o-medo-da-demolicao/"],["RTP (\"We are Almada too\")","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/tambem-somos-almada-moradores-do-bairro-da-penajoia-escrevem-carta-a-camara-municipal_n1693112"],["DN (IHRU guarantee)","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/almada-ihru-garante-que-nao-havera-demolicoes-sem-solucoes-habitacionais"]],"stat":"About 350 people, 60 children, without water or public electricity on state-owned land","link":"https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2024/12/10/bairro-da-penajoia-almada-se-tivesse-outras-condicoes-nao-estava-aqui/404757/","linkL":"Read on Renascença"},"revive-forte-outao":{"corpo":"<p>Under the Revive programme, which grants private companies concessions to run publicly-owned properties of historical value, the Forte Velho do Outão (also known as the 7th Outão Battery) — a former coastal defence battery inside the Arrábida Natural Park, next to the Secil quarries — was granted for 50 years.</p>\n<p>The contract was signed on 25 August 2023 with Real Bolhão, Restaurantes, Unipessoal, Lda., with a minimum annual rent of €130,987.32 and a construction area of 6,909 m². Press reports put the actual contracted rent at close to €201,000 a year. The 2022 tender allowed for a hotel, local accommodation or another tourism project; the concession was initially announced for a restaurant. In February 2025, Setúbal City Council approved a reconversion of the project into a 5-star hotel with around 35 rooms.</p>\n<p>According to the official Revive page, operations are expected to start by September 2027. There is no public confirmation of works having started on site.</p>","fontes":[["Turismo de Portugal (Revive, official tender page)", "https://revive.turismodeportugal.pt/pt-pt/node/939"], ["ECO (concession and rent)", "https://eco.sapo.pt/2023/09/12/7a-bateria-do-outao-na-serra-da-arrabida-vai-ser-transformado-em-restaurante-com-renda-anual-de-200-mil-euros/"], ["O Setubalense (2023, restaurant)", "https://osetubalense.com/local/setubal/vai-nascer-um-restaurante-na-7-a-bateria-do-outao/"], ["Publituris Hotelaria (2025, reconversion into hotel)", "https://publiturishotelaria.pt/2025/02/04/camara-de-setubal-aprova-reconversao-da-7-a-bataria-do-outao-em-empreendimento-turistico"], ["O Setubalense (2025, hotel approval)", "https://osetubalense.com/local/setubal/camara-municipal-aprova-proposta-para-futuro-hotel-na-7-a-bataria-do-outao/"], ["Echo Boomer", "https://echoboomer.pt/7a-bateria-do-outao-vai-dar-origem-novo-restaurante/"]],"stat":"50-year concession, next to the Secil quarries","link":"https://revive.turismodeportugal.pt/pt-pt/node/939","linkL":"See tender on Revive →"},"barragem-foupana":{"corpo":"<p>Portugal's Environment Agency (APA) opened, on 31 August 2026, public consultation on the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) for the new Foupana dam in eastern Algarve, running until 12 October via the Participa portal. The project, promoted by the Eastern Algarve Irrigation Beneficiaries Association (ABPRSA), includes the dam itself, a connecting tunnel to the Odeleite-Beliche system and access roads, with an overall estimated cost between 150 and 200 million euros.</p><p>Environmental group Almargem has opposed the project since 2023, calling the Foupana stream &quot;the Algarve's last great free-flowing stream&quot; and one of the region's best-preserved watercourses, with no protection status at all. The group argues the Foupana should be included in the Natura 2000 network, warns of the impact on the saramugo, a critically endangered endemic fish, and notes that the Algarve's six existing dams (Odelouca, Arade, Funcho, Bravura, Beliche and Odeleite) already frequently run below capacity, questioning the cost-benefit of a seventh. Castro Marim's municipal council has separately warned about the lack of protected status for the area, compounded by a mining prospecting request overlapping the future dam's site.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal do Algarve / Lusa (opening of public consultation)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/apa-avanca-com-avaliacao-de-impacte-ambiental-para-barragem-na-foupana/"],["Algarve Marafado (estimated project cost)","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/08/29/nova-barragem-a-vista-para-o-algarve-custo-ronda-os-200-milhoes-de-euros/"],["Jornal do Algarve (Almargem's position)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/almargem-manifesta-se-contra-construcao-da-barragem-da-foupana/"],["Barlavento (Castro Marim council on the area's vulnerability)","https://www.barlavento.pt/barragem-da-foupana-castro-marim-alerta-para-vunerabilidade-da-zona/"]],"stat":"Estimated cost between 150 and 200 million euros","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/barragem-da-foupana","linkL":"See public consultation on Participa →"},"castanheira-ribatejo":{"corpo":"<p>Vila Franca de Xira City Council approved, on 25 August 2026, moving ahead with a detailed plan that expands the Lisbon-North Logistics Platform in Castanheira do Ribatejo by around 340 hectares — nearly triple the current area of about 100 hectares, occupied since 2008. Around 300 hectares are earmarked for economic activities (logistics, technology and data centres), with the area closest to the Tejo river becoming a riverside urban park. The process was in public consultation until 4 September 2026.</p><p>The CDU (Communist coalition) criticised converting about 295 hectares of farmland and ecologically valuable land, estimating €491 million in land-value gains for owners and developers from the reclassification. PSD and IL called for stronger guarantees on the power grid, needed for the planned data centres, and Chega demanded assurances on infrastructure and firefighting capacity. Mayor Fernando Paulo Ferreira argues the project will create around 5,000 jobs and promises a strategic environmental assessment before proceeding. In an earlier phase of the same project (2021-2022), Quercus and the civic movement XIRADANIA had already issued a negative opinion on the environmental impact study for a roughly 38-hectare subdivision on the same platform, citing insufficient study of alternative locations and downplaying of contamination risk to the country's largest freshwater aquifer.</p>","fontes":[["idealista/news (announcement of the detailed plan)","https://www.idealista.pt/news/imobiliario/empresas/2026/08/31/77390-vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-de-lisboa-norte"],["Público (opposition's position on the council)","https://www.publico.pt/2026/08/26/local/noticia/vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-lisboanorte-oposicao-coloca-duvidas-2186059"],["Participa.pt (public consultation for the earlier project phase, 2021-2022)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/plataforma-logistica-de-castanheira-do-ribatejo"],["Quercus (negative opinion on the earlier project phase, 2021)","https://quercus.pt/2021/03/plataforma-logistica-de-castanheira-do-ribatejo-quercus-da-parecer-negativo/"]],"stat":"340-hectare detailed plan, about 300 for logistics, technology and data centres","link":"https://www.idealista.pt/news/imobiliario/empresas/2026/08/31/77390-vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-de-lisboa-norte","linkL":"Read the article →"},"campismo-gale":{"corpo":"<p>The Galé campsite in Melides (Grândola municipality) closed in October 2021, after being bought for around €25 million by Discovery Land Company, the developer behind the Costa Terra Golf &amp; Ocean Club luxury resort. Widely regarded as the country's best public campsite, it has never reopened.</p><p>The Reabrir a Galé civic movement, born from a group of regular campsite users, collected over 12,000 signatures on a petition for the campsite's continued operation, discussed at a parliamentary hearing in October 2022 with the participation of the Dunas Livres Association. The group also alleges environmental irregularities linked to the resort, such as dune destruction to build a golf course roughly 500 metres from the sea. Grândola's municipal council has stated it cannot intervene since it is private investment. The same resort — and the same stretch of coast between Tróia and Melides — is also linked to recurring complaints about restricted public beach access, documented in official inspections and denounced by Quercus.</p>","fontes":[["Rádio Campanário (parliamentary hearing)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/reabertura-do-parque-de-campismo-da-gale-em-audicao-na-assembleia-da-republica-dia-13/"],["The Portugal News (profile of the Reabrir a Galé movement)","https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2022-08-06/reabrir-a-gale-fighting-for-answers/69191"],["Portugal Resident (barriers to beach access in Melides)","https://www.portugalresident.com/all-portuguese-beaches-are-public-says-government-but-not-so-in-melides/"]],"stat":"Closed since October 2021 · petition with over 12,000 signatures","link":"https://www.facebook.com/ReabrirAGale/","linkL":"See the Reabrir a Galé movement's page →"},"sobreiros-tortosendo":{"corpo":"<p>Quercus denounced, in a statement sent to newsrooms on 1 September 2026, Covilhã City Council's intention to fell around 1,400 cork oaks — dozens of them centuries old — to allow the expansion of the Tortosendo Industrial Park, as part of the revision of the Municipal Master Plan (PDM). The environmental group points to two watercourses, three ponds and several springs in the planned area, plus 10 primary residences whose occupants could face expropriation. The denunciation comes days before the end of the PDM revision's public discussion period, which closes on 4 September 2026.</p><p>Quercus questions the need for more industrial land, arguing the current industrial zone \"has half its plots empty or abandoned\", and calls the expansion a \"false pretext\". The group argues that, since it involves a legally protected species, the council must prove the expansion into the cork oak stand is \"the only viable alternative to serve the public interest\" before authorising its removal. Mayor Hélio Fazendeiro confirms this third phase of the industrial park was already planned around 30 years ago, acknowledges the environmental and family concerns, and says the expansion will comply with the law, including replanting trees as happened in earlier phases of the same park.</p>","fontes":[["Observador (Quercus denunciation, in Portuguese)", "https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/"], ["Rádio Clube da Covilhã (mayor's response, in Portuguese)", "https://radio-covilha.pt/2026/09/noticias/quercus-denuncia-possivel-abate-de-sobreiros-no-tortosendo-camara-garante-cumprimento-da-lei/"], ["Greensavers / SAPO Ambiente (in Portuguese)", "https://greensavers.sapo.pt/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/"], ["Ambiente Magazine (in Portuguese)", "https://www.ambientemagazine.com/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-do-parque-industrial-do-tortosendo/"]],"stat":"Master plan would fell around 1,400 cork oaks, dozens centuries old","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/","linkL":"Read the article (in Portuguese) →"},"artilharia-um-campolide":{"corpo":"<p>The former Artilharia Um barracks in Campolide gave way to a real-estate project of seven plots and 683 housing units, developed by Novo Banco, on about five hectares next to Amoreiras.</p>\n<p>The Artilharia Um Movement contests the Environmental Impact Assessment exemption granted to the project, even though it exceeds the legal 500-unit threshold that normally requires such a study, and filed a formal complaint with the European Commission against the Portuguese State.</p>\n<p>A residents' petition, with over 400 signatures, is being reviewed by Lisbon's Municipal Assembly, while the case is also being examined by the Public Prosecutor's Office.</p>","fontes":[["Observador (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/08/18/movimento-civico-artilharia-um-queixa-se-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-urbanistico-em-lisboa/"],["ECO (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/07/moradores-de-lisboa-lancam-peticao-contra-projeto-urbanistico-na-zona-das-amoreiras/"],["Notícias de Lisboa (in Portuguese)","https://noticiaslx.pt/2026/08/18/queixa-a-comissao-europeia-lisboa/"]],"stat":"683 housing units · exempted from EIA","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=artilharia-um","linkL":"See the petition"},"fortes-ferreira-alentejo":{"corpo":"<p>The AZPO – Azeites de Portugal plant, which extracts olive-pomace oil about 300 metres from the village of Fortes in Ferreira do Alentejo, has been accused for over a decade of polluting the region's air and water; the Portuguese Environment Agency has already confirmed unlicensed wastewater discharges.</p>\n<p>A criminal case against the company was archived by the Public Prosecutor's Office for lack of evidence. Tired of waiting for a response from the authorities, the Amigos das Fortes Environmental Association bought its own air-quality monitoring equipment.</p>\n<p>Between 24 and 29 July 2026, the equipment recorded over 30 hours of volatile organic compound concentrations above acceptable limits. The association will hand the results over to the environment agency and has launched a petition for the right to breathe clean air.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/portugal/queixas-no-ministerio-publico-contra-fabrica-acusada-de-poluir-aldeia-no-alentejo-9345952.html"],["Observador (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/24/cansados-de-esperar-moradores-compram-equipamento-para-medir-poluicao-de-fabrica-junto-a-sua-aldeia-no-alentejo/"],["Plataforma Media (in Portuguese)","https://www.plataformamedia.com/2026/08/03/qualidade-do-ar-preocupa-moradores-de-aldeia-portuguesa-apos-testes-revelarem-valores-acima-do-permitido/"]],"stat":"30+ hours above VOC limits","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT131002","linkL":"See the petition"},"biometano-abrigada-alenquer":{"corpo":"<p>The company Gás da Terra wants to build a €20.5 million biomethane plant in Marés, about 500 metres from homes in Abrigada, Alenquer municipality, to process around 84,000 tonnes of agricultural and livestock waste a year.</p>\n<p>At a public meeting in August 2026, at the Sociedade Filarmónica União e Progresso de Abrigada, residents repeatedly interrupted the company's presentation, rejecting the project over fears of bad odours — a problem they say they already suffer from — and increased heavy-vehicle traffic.</p>\n<p>Alenquer municipal council issued an unfavourable opinion on 26 August. The public consultation runs on participa.pt until 15 September 2026.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante (in Portuguese)","https://omirante.pt/sociedade/2026-08-15-abrigada-rejeita-unidade-de-biometano-a-500-metros-das-casas-6d2e6bf7"],["Voz de Alenquer (in Portuguese)","https://vozdealenquer.pt/futura-central-de-biometano-nas-mares-apresentada-com-contestacao-de-populares/"],["Valor Local (in Portuguese)","https://valorlocal.pt/projeto-biometano-mares-alenquer-preocupa-populacao/"]],"stat":"€20.5 million · 500m from homes","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/uab-abrigada--unidade-de-producao-de-biometano-de-origem-renovavel-de-abrigada_185","linkL":"Join the public consultation →"},"cais-carga-sines":{"corpo":"<p>The Environmental Impact Study for the new General Cargo Dock at the Port of Sines, a €90 million investment promoted by the Administration of the Ports of Sines and the Algarve, sets out \"dual\" civil and military use requirements for the infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The Left Bloc questioned the government about the terms, scale and timeline of any military use, and whether the new dock is part of a wider strategy linking it to NATO's logistics network. The port authority denies a permanent military installation.</p>\n<p>Iniciativa Cidadã, a Sines residents' group led by Eugénia Santa Bárbara and Bruno Candeias, organised a public meeting on 4 September 2026 at the Sines Fire Station, arguing there had not been enough public information before the Environmental Impact Assessment's public consultation.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/pol%C3%ADtica/be-questiona-governo-se-novo-cais-de-sines-far-parte-da-rede-logstica-da-nato"],["Sul Informação (in Portuguese)","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2026/09/possivel-utilizacao-militar-do-novo-cais-do-porto-de-sines-preocupa-cidadaos"],["Esquerda.net (in Portuguese)","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/bloco-contra-cais-militar-em-sines/98744"],["Participa.pt (public consultation)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/novo-cais-de-carga-geral-do-porto-de-sines"]],"stat":"€90 million · \"dual\" use","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/novo-cais-de-carga-geral-do-porto-de-sines","linkL":"🗳 Join the public consultation →"},"costa-caparica-arvores":{"corpo":"<p>A beach-access upgrade project in Costa da Caparica (phase 2), costing around €3 million, led Almada municipal council to announce the felling of 47 trees in Praça Padre Manuel Bernardes and Torre das Argolas.</p>\n<p>Residents, however, count 103 trees already cut or marked for felling, including at least 23 in June 2026 alone, and question the council's criteria. The council has pledged to plant 120 new trees in compensation.</p>\n<p>A public petition, now past 2,600 signatures, calls for an immediate halt to the felling of the 34 trees still marked, for the demolition of Praça dos Navegantes to stop, and for more transparency and dialogue with residents before the works proceed.</p>","fontes":[["Almadense (in Portuguese)","https://almadense.sapo.pt/ambiente/abate-de-arvores-na-costa-da-caparica-indigna-moradores-nao-percebemos-qual-o-criterio/"],["Almada Municipal Council (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-almada.pt/empreitada-acessibilidade-a-costa-da-caparica-acesso-alternativo-as-praias-fase-2-rua-padre-manuel-bernardes"]],"stat":"103 trees counted vs. 47 announced","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT132029","linkL":"See the petition"},"meco-sesimbra-agua-turismo":{"corpo":"<p>Since 2021, residents of Aldeia do Meco, in Sesimbra, have opposed four large tourism projects — including TURIMECO's \"Pinhal do Atlântico\" aparthotel, with 411 units and 1,168 beds — which together plan around 600 dwellings and over 1,800 beds for a village with just over 300 inhabitants, in an area classified as a Site of Community Importance (Arrábida/Espichel).</p>\n<p>A petition delivered to Parliament, with thousands of signatures, warns of the impact on biodiversity, on already-difficult access and parking, and on water resources already scarce in summer.</p>\n<p>A new petition now demands an embargo and revocation of these developments' licences over the risk of salinizing the aquifer: according to official environment agency data cited in the petition, the water exploitation index in the coastal sub-basins between the Tagus and Sado reaches 93% in September, with the piezometric level of the Tagus/Left Bank basin already below the 20th percentile.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/local/turismo-populacao-do-meco-contra-mais-1832-camas-na-aldeia-em-unidades-turisticas-13751017.html"],["MAGG (in Portuguese)","https://magg.sapo.pt/atualidade/atualidade-nacional/artigos/aldeia-meco-lanca-peticao-projetos-hoteleiros"],["Notícias ao Minuto (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/casa/1752440/ha-uma-nova-peticao-nao-a-grandes-projetos-hoteleiros-aldeia-do-meco"]],"stat":"600+ dwellings · 1,800+ beds planned","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=aguaemsesimbra","linkL":"See the water petition"},"incineradora-algarve":{"corpo": "<p>Environment and Energy Minister Maria da Graça Carvalho announced on 8 August 2026 that the Portuguese Environment Agency will move ahead with an energy-from-waste incineration unit in the Algarve, with investment of up to 300 million euros and operation expected to begin in 2034. The plan responds to the looming exhaustion of the Portimão and Loulé landfills, expected around 2027, in a region that produces 400,000 tonnes of urban waste a year, 85% of which goes to landfill.</p><p>Environmental group Zero called the proposal \"harmful management\" of the public interest and requested an urgent meeting with the minister to clarify the region's waste strategy. Quercus considers incineration \"completely anachronistic\", incompatible with PERSU 2030 targets and Portugal's climate commitments, arguing the technology emits more CO₂ per kWh than fossil fuels.</p><p>On 3 September, Quercus announced it will lead a White Paper on Waste in Portugal, with input from universities, municipalities and other bodies, to propose alternatives to incineration. The Environment Agency plans to launch a tender on 15 October to study the technology and final location of the unit.</p>", "fontes": [["Observador — Ambientalistas consideram incineradora \"gestão danosa\"", "https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/ambientalistas-consideram-incineradora-no-algarve-gestao-danosa-do-interesse-publico/"], ["TSF — Governo anuncia construção de incineradora no Algarve", "https://www.tsf.pt/sociedade/artigo/governo-anuncia-construcao-de-incineradora-no-algarve/18114431"], ["Barlavento — ZERO chama gestão danosa à eventual incineradora", "https://www.barlavento.pt/zero-chama-gestao-danosa-a-eventual-incineradora-no-algarve/"], ["Quercus — Queimar lixo não", "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/03/queimar-lixo-nao-quercus-critica-incineradora-no-algarve-e-vai-dinamizar-livro-branco-dos-residuos-em-portugal/"], ["Sul Informação — Quercus rejeita incineradora e exige respostas à ministra", "https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/09/quercus-rejeita-incineradora-no-algarve-e-exige-respostas-a-ministra/"]], "stat": "400,000 tonnes of waste/year in the Algarve, 85% landfilled", "link": "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/03/queimar-lixo-nao-quercus-critica-incineradora-no-algarve-e-vai-dinamizar-livro-branco-dos-residuos-em-portugal/", "linkL": "See Quercus's position →"},"matosinhos-ribeira-leca":{"corpo": "<p>Discharges of polluting waste from the site of Galp's former refinery in Leça da Palmeira left a \"nauseating smell\" affecting Matosinhos in April 2026. Galp confirmed the occurrence at a decommissioned part of the old refinery, saying it was \"under mitigation\" and posed no risk to public health; the Portuguese Environment Agency is now processing a fine against the company.</p><p>The problem runs deeper: Matosinhos City Council has detected around 900 illegal connections discharging wastewater directly into the Riguinha and Carcavelos streams, which flow out near Matosinhos beach. Episodes of microbiological contamination have already led to temporary bathing bans — the beach was closed 18 times in the last bathing season — and it risks losing its official \"Bathing Water\" status.</p><p>In August 2026, PSD and Chega councillors demanded the council draw up an integrated stream-recovery plan, inspect illegal connections and set up public real-time water-quality monitoring. The municipality has already corrected around 200 of the illegal connections found.</p>", "fontes": [["JN — Descargas nas ribeiras deixam \"cheiro nauseabundo\" em Matosinhos", "https://www.jn.pt/jn-direto/artigo/descargas-nas-ribeiras-deixam-cheiro-nauseabundo-em-matosinhos/18069284"], ["Observador — Galp confirma descarga de antiga refinaria em Matosinhos \"em mitigação\"", "https://observador.pt/2026/05/06/galp-confirma-descarga-de-antiga-refinaria-em-matosinhos-que-esta-em-mitigacao/"], ["ECO — Galp confirma descarga de antiga refinaria em Matosinhos", "https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/06/galp-confirma-descarga-de-antiga-refinaria-em-matosinhos-que-esta-em-mitigacao/"], ["JN — Matosinhos deteta 900 ligações ilegais nas ribeiras urbanas", "https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/matosinhos-deteta-900-ligacoes-ilegais-nas-ribeiras-urbanas/17853601"], ["Público — Praia de Matosinhos em risco de não ser zona balnear", "https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/25/azul/noticia/praia-matosinhos-risco-nao-zona-balnear-2162430"], ["JN — Centenas de ligações ilegais ajudam a explicar contaminação na praia de Matosinhos", "https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/centenas-de-ligacoes-ilegais-ajudam-a-explicar-contaminacao-na-praia-de-matosinhos-/17858641"]], "stat": "~900 illegal connections found in Matosinhos's streams", "link": "https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/matosinhos-deteta-900-ligacoes-ilegais-nas-ribeiras-urbanas/17853601", "linkL": "See JN report →"},"pedreira-cerro-meio-tavira":{"corpo": "<p>The Tavira Court ordered the immediate and permanent closure of the \"Cerro do Meio\" quarry, operated by Miner Blanc, Lda. (Verdasca group), in the Luz de Tavira and Santo Estêvão parish union. A group of residents had filed a special personality-rights protection case asking for the activity — suspended since 2013 and resumed in 2025 — to be shut down entirely.</p><p>Residents' complaints centred on excessive noise, vibration and dust. The court also found that vibrations and earthmoving in the area could damage an essential water-supply pipeline for the eastern Algarve that runs near the quarry.</p><p>The company was given 24 hours to halt operations, on pain of a disobedience offence.</p>", "fontes": [["Jornal do Algarve — Tribunal de Tavira dá razão a moradores e condena empresa a encerrar pedreira", "https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/tribunal-de-tavira-da-razao-a-moradores-e-condena-empresa-a-encerrar-pedreira/"], ["Correio da Manhã — Tribunal manda encerrar pedreira após queixas de excesso de ruído e poeiras", "https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/tribunal-manda-encerrar-pedreira-apos-queixas-de-excesso-de-ruido-e-poeiras"], ["Postal — Pedreira de Tavira encerrada após tribunal considerar violados direitos dos moradores", "https://postal.pt/algarve/pedreira-de-tavira-encerrada-apos-tribunal-considerar-violados-direitos-dos-moradores/"]], "stat": "Immediate court-ordered closure by the Tavira Court", "link": "https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/tribunal-de-tavira-da-razao-a-moradores-e-condena-empresa-a-encerrar-pedreira/", "linkL": "See Jornal do Algarve report →"},"royal-china-clay-serra-del-rei":{"corpo": "<p>Mining concession C-185 \"Royal China Clay\", awarded to Motamineral – Minerais Industriais, S.A., aims to extract around 101 hectares of kaolinitic sand and clay across three sites near Serra d'El-Rei, in the municipality of Peniche, with an on-site washing plant. The extracted material is destined for the ceramic-paste factory of MCS – Mota Ceramic Solutions.</p><p>The public consultation on the environmental impact study ran from 22 July to 1 September 2026. According to Quercus, the concession would affect 471 of the 662 cork oaks in the area, with compensation planned for just 300 new specimens — which the group calls \"derisory\" — as well as nine vulnerable animal species, a wet-heathland habitat and the native plant Drosophyllum lusitanicum.</p><p>The Óbidos and Peniche municipal councils, the Atouguia da Baleia, Peniche and Serra d'El-Rei parish councils, Quercus and the Portuguese Association of Landscape Architects all issued unfavourable opinions on the project. The Left Bloc questioned the government about the process on 3 September.</p>", "fontes": [["DN — Óbidos e Peniche contestam exploração mineira de caulino e argila a céu aberto", "https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/bidos-e-peniche-contra-explorao-mineira-de-caulino-e-argila-a-cu-aberto"], ["Quercus — Quercus insta a CIM Oeste a posicionar-se contra exploração mineira em Peniche", "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/28/exploracao-mineira-peniche/"], ["Observador — Bloco de Esquerda questiona Governo sobre projeto de mina de caulino para Peniche", "https://observador.pt/2026/09/03/bloco-de-esquerda-questiona-governo-sobre-projeto-de-mina-de-caulino-para-peniche/"], ["Região de Leiria — Câmaras de Peniche e Óbidos contestam exploração mineira em Serra d'El-Rei", "https://www.regiaodeleiria.pt/2026/08/camaras-de-peniche-e-obidos-contestam-exploracao-mineira-em-serra-del-rei/"], ["Observador — Arquitetos paisagistas chumbam mina de caulino em Peniche", "https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/arquitetos-paisagistas-chumbam-mina-de-caulino-em-peniche-abate-de-sobreiros-sem-compensacao-e-lacuna-mais-consequente/"]], "stat": "471 of 662 cork oaks affected, compensation of only 300 new trees", "link": "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/28/exploracao-mineira-peniche/", "linkL": "See Quercus's position →"},"barragem-pisao":{"corpo": "<p>The Pisão Dam, budgeted at over 220 million euros, would submerge the village of Pisão, in the municipality of Crato, Alto Alentejo. Since 2022, four environmental groups — GEOTA, Quercus, LPN and ZERO — have challenged the project's public-interest justification in court, arguing that public water supply would account for barely 1% of the future reservoir's annual volume, against 65% for agricultural use.</p><p>Construction began in September 2025 and has been repeatedly suspended and resumed: in January 2026 the Castelo Branco Administrative and Fiscal Court allowed work to resume, but the Southern Central Administrative Court overturned that ruling in May over a procedural error, sending the case back to the lower court and reinstating the suspension of the Environmental Impact Declaration.</p><p>The Southern Central Administrative Court's ruling does not assess the dam's environmental or technical merits, only a procedural issue — but in practice it has kept construction halted.</p>", "fontes": [["Público — Obras da Barragem do Pisão voltam a ficar suspensas", "https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/18/local/noticia/obras-barragem-pisao-voltam-ficar-suspensas-2175113"], ["Público — Autarcas dizem que tribunal levantou suspensão das obras da Barragem do Pisão", "https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/31/azul/noticia/autarcas-tribunal-levantou-suspensao-obras-barragem-pisao-2162956"], ["Renascença — Ambientalistas requerem em tribunal paragem das obras na Barragem do Pisão", "https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/03/20/ambientalistas-requerem-em-tribunal-paragem-das-obras-na-barragem-do-pisao/463818/"], ["Agroportal — Questão processual implica nova suspensão das obras da Barragem do Pisão", "https://www.agroportal.pt/questao-processual-implica-nova-suspensao-das-obras-da-barragem-do-pisao/"]], "stat": "Over 220 million euros; only 1% of volume for public supply", "link": "https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/18/local/noticia/obras-barragem-pisao-voltam-ficar-suspensas-2175113", "linkL": "See Público report →"},"mata-albergaria-volta":{"corpo": "<p>ICNF authorised the 7th stage of the Volta a Portugal cycling race to pass through the Mata da Albergaria, one of the country's few well-preserved native oak forests, inside Portugal's only National Park (Peneda-Gerês). The area includes partial-protection zones and is bordered in part by total-protection zones.</p><p>The authorisation imposed strict conditions: no public access, no sound amplification, no aerial support and support vehicles kept to a minimum. Even so, Quercus challenged the decision, warning that the impacts are not eliminated and that it sets a \"grave precedent\" for future events in protected areas. ZERO said it was satisfied with the \"strong conditions\" imposed.</p><p>The stage went ahead on 13 August 2026 under those conditions; Quercus continues to demand the stretch be excluded from future editions of the race.</p>", "fontes": [["Observador — Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal em mata sensível no Gerês e alerta para \"grave precedente\"", "https://observador.pt/2026/08/11/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-em-mata-sensivel-no-geres-e-alerta-para-grave-precedente/"], ["Quercus — Mata de Albergaria, no Gerês, não é lugar para a passagem da Volta a Portugal em bicicleta", "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/11/mata-de-albergaria-no-geres-nao-e-lugar-para-a-passagem-da-volta-a-portugal-em-bicicleta/"], ["Renascença — Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal no Gerês, ZERO satisfeita com \"fortes condicionantes\"", "https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/08/11/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-no-geres-zero-satisfeita-com-fortes-condicionantes/481484/"], ["A Bola — Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal no Gerês e pede suspensão da etapa", "https://www.abola.pt/noticias/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-no-geres-e-pede-suspensao-da-etapa-2026081111344648856"]], "stat": "The only well-preserved native oak forest in Portugal's only National Park", "link": "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/11/mata-de-albergaria-no-geres-nao-e-lugar-para-a-passagem-da-volta-a-portugal-em-bicicleta/", "linkL": "See Quercus's position →"},"agueda-eucaliptos":{"corpo": "<p>Quercus's Aveiro regional branch is denouncing new eucalyptus plantations near homes, waterways and roads in parts of the Águeda municipality hit by the 2024 wildfires, including a plot adjoining the home of a victim of the September 2024 fire. The GNR's SEPNA nature-protection service confirmed the existence of authorisations issued by ICNF under the legal framework for afforestation and reforestation actions.</p><p>Quercus is demanding ICNF urgently revoke licences in sensitive areas, inspect existing plantations, suspend or reverse risky situations, and follow through on measures announced after the 2024 fires to convert the landscape. </p><p>Águeda's municipal council says it set clear restrictions on fast-growing forest species in sensitive areas through its Municipal Master Plan, but accuses ICNF of systematically ignoring those rules when issuing afforestation permits.</p>", "fontes": [["Quercus — Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto no concelho de Águeda em áreas afetadas pelos incêndios", "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/09/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-no-concelho-de-agueda-em-areas-afetadas-pelos-incendios/"], ["Agroportal — Quercus quer revogação das licenças de plantação de eucaliptos em Águeda", "https://www.agroportal.pt/quercus-quer-revogacao-das-licencas-de-plantacao-de-eucaliptos-em-agueda/"], ["Notícias de Águeda — Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto em zonas sensíveis de Águeda", "https://noticiasdeagueda.sapo.pt/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-em-zonas-sensiveis-de-agueda-e-pede-revisao-urgente-das-autorizacoes/"], ["Jornal da Bairrada — Águeda: Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto em áreas de incêndios", "https://www.jb.pt/2026/07/agueda-quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-em-areas-de-incendios/"]], "stat": "Plantations next to the home of a September 2024 fire victim", "link": "https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/09/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-no-concelho-de-agueda-em-areas-afetadas-pelos-incendios/", "linkL": "See Quercus statement →"},"meia-praia-lagos":{"corpo": "<p>Around 50 people protested outside Lagos City Council against the construction of two hotels and a block of tourist apartments on 11,000 m² of Meia Praia, under a 1988 building permit revised in 2008. The protest was organised by the civic movement \"Salvar a Meia Praia\" (Save Meia Praia), made up mostly of foreign residents in the area.</p><p>The movement argues the land should be turned into public green space rather than a tourist development that includes a five-star hotel. It is also calling for a new environmental impact assessment, particularly of the lagoon basin on the site.</p><p>Lagos's mayor said he was not in favour of building on the first line of coast, but acknowledged the council cannot block the project if the developer meets all applicable laws and regulations; he confirmed licensing is conditional on rehabilitating the lagoon basin.</p>", "fontes": [["Postal — Protesto em Lagos pede suspensão de projeto turístico na Meia Praia", "https://postal.pt/algarve/protesto-em-lagos-pede-suspensao-de-projeto-turistico-na-meia-praia/"], ["Jornal do Algarve — Cidadãos mostram-se contra a construção de unidades hoteleiras na Meia Praia, em Lagos", "https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/cidadaos-mostram-se-contra-a-construcao-de-unidades-hoteleiras-na-meia-praia-em-lagos/"], ["The Portugal News — Citizens gather at Câmara Municipal de Lagos to Save Meia Praia", "https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2026-08-28/citizens-gather-at-camara-municipal-de-lagos-to-save-meia-praia/1075492"], ["Algarve Marafado — O caos urbanístico da Meia Praia", "https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/04/30/o-caos-urbanistico-da-meia-praia/"]], "stat": "Two hotels and tourist apartments on 11,000 m² of Meia Praia", "link": "https://postal.pt/algarve/protesto-em-lagos-pede-suspensao-de-projeto-turistico-na-meia-praia/", "linkL": "See report on the protest →"},"litoral-greenpeace":{"corpo": "<p>The report \"Destruição a Toda a Costa — Retrato de um litoral português em risco\" (\"Destruction All Along the Coast\"), published by Greenpeace Portugal on 23 July 2026, finds that 25% of mainland Portugal's coastline is eroding and that more than 100,000 people live in at-risk coastal areas, as sea level rises 3.7 mm a year — faster than the global average.</p><p>The organisation singles out the municipalities of Sesimbra and Grândola, in Setúbal district, as examples of outdated municipal master plans that keep licensing large tourism developments in protected areas: in Sesimbra, projects such as Pinhal da Prata, Pinhal do Atlântico and Étosoto occupy more than 260 hectares of protected land, moving forward without adequate environmental assessment.</p><p>Greenpeace estimates that by 2100 up to 50% of Alentejo's beaches and around 40% of the Algarve's beaches could disappear, and is calling on the government for a moratorium on construction in flood- or erosion-risk areas until 2050.</p>", "fontes": [["Greenpeace Portugal — Comunicado do relatório \"Destruição a Toda a Costa\"", "https://www.greenpeace.pt/meios-de-comunicacao/comunicados/greenpeace-portugal-alerta-um-quarto-da-costa-continental-portuguesa-esta-em-recuo-e-pressao-urbanistica-agrava-risco-no-litoral/"], ["Jornal Económico — 25% da costa portuguesa está a recuar e mais de 100 mil pessoas vivem em risco", "https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/25-da-costa-portuguesa-esta-a-recuar-e-mais-de-100-mil-pessoas-vivem-em-risco/"], ["Barlavento — Greenpeace Portugal pede travão à construção nas zonas de risco do litoral algarvio", "https://www.barlavento.pt/greenpeace-construcao-zonas-risco-litoral-algarvio/"], ["Executive Digest — Mar avança sobre o litoral português e 40% das praias podem desaparecer até ao fim do século", "https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/mar-avanca-sobre-o-litoral-portugues-e-40-das-praias-podem-desaparecer-ate-ao-fim-do-seculo/"]], "stat": "25% of the mainland coast eroding; 100,000+ people at risk", "link": "https://www.greenpeace.pt/como-ajudar/peticoes/litoral/", "linkL": "See Greenpeace's petition →"},"eolico-penamacor-2":{"corpo": "<p>The government authorised, through Order (Despacho) no. 775/2026 of 23 January, the felling of 451 cork oaks (383 young, 68 mature) and 304 holm oaks (284 young, 20 mature) — 755 protected trees in total — across 6.76 hectares in the Serra de Santo André, in the Meimoa and Penamacor parishes, Castelo Branco district.</p><p>The felling is for the Penamacor 2 Wind Farm repowering project: developer Lestenergia will replace the seven existing turbines with four more powerful ones, nearly quadrupling annual output from 23.48 GWh to 88.44 GWh. The Portuguese Environment Agency exempted the project from its own environmental impact assessment, under the regime applicable to repowering already-licensed wind farms.</p><p>The authorisation is conditional on an environmental compensation plan requiring the company to plant trees across 12.7 hectares — almost double the affected area. A public petition is calling for the felling authorisation to be revoked entirely, for alternative, lower-impact sites to be assessed, and for the principle of avoiding and minimising harm before compensating for it to be reinforced.</p>", "fontes": [["Público — Governo autoriza abate de sobreiros e azinheiras em parque eólico em Penamacor", "https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/27/azul/noticia/governo-autoriza-abate-sobreiros-azinheiras-parque-eolico-penamacor-2162560"], ["Executive Digest — Governo autoriza abate de mais de 9000 árvores protegidas em apenas dois meses", "https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/governo-autoriza-abate-de-mais-de-9000-arvores-protegidas-em-apenas-dois-meses/"], ["Diário Digital Castelo Branco — Penamacor: Governo autoriza abate de sobreiros e azinheiras em parque eólico", "https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/70664/penamacor-governo-autoriza-abate-de-sobreiros-e-azinheiras-em-parque-eolico"], ["Despacho n.º 775/2026, de 23 de janeiro — Diário da República", "https://dre.tretas.org/dre/6421708/despacho-775-2026-de-23-de-janeiro"]], "stat": "755 protected trees authorised for felling (451 cork oaks, 304 holm oaks)", "link": "https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT129537", "linkL": "See the public petition →"}};